{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CHBHfeKGaAsz3SwG9sLmSw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'C1（+34.0pp, 5 models, perturbation PASS）+ C4（model×type interaction,\n2\t  auth_scope 52pp range）承载论文核心贡献。 C5 从 \"validated taxonomy\" 降级为 \"convergent LLM-coded\n3\t  and human evidence with moderate agreement (κ=0.39)\"； abstract 将 \"type-diagnostic\n4\t  failure signatures\" 替换为 \"type-associated failure patterns\"； Contribution (3) 保留\n5\t  \"supported by\" 但追加 \"preliminary human validation (κ=0.39)\" 限定语。 C3 layer effect\n6\t  不再作为独立 finding，降为 C4 下属观察（\"model×type interaction subsumes the aggregate layer gap\"）。\n7\t  SOPBench 描述为 \"partial cross-domain evidence (Δ=19.4pp, 4/5 models replicate)\" 而非\n8\t  \"full replication\"； DeepSeek 在 SOPBench 上 Δ=12.4pp 归因于 rule-based verifier 的 domain-specific\n9\t  校准差异，不构成 fundamental non-replication。 Rebuttal 策略：强调 κ=0.39 超过 chance 且与已知 category-boundary\n10\t  ambiguity（auth_scope/incompleteness）一致； 4-type dominant mode 一致性覆盖了理论上最具区分性的类型（scopal,\n11\t  lexical, CP）。 κ=0.39 比纯 automated coding（LLM-LLM κ=0.517）低，但 human inter-annotator\n12\t  在 failure mode 编码上天然更分散； collapsed 4-category scheme κ=0.44 接近 moderate。 竞争力：C1\n13\t  causal design + C4 interaction 足够支撑 novel contribution；weakened C5 不致命但限制 main-track\n14\t  award potential。 Expected ARR: 3.75（competitive for EMNLP Findings / borderline\n15\t  Main poster）。\n16\t\n17\t  '\n18\timagined_experiments:\n19\t- name: full_study_clause_generation\n20\t  plan_id: plan_001\n21\t  description: 生成并验证 300 条 clause pairs (50/type × 6 types)，含新类型 coreferential 和 authorization_scope\n22\t    各 50 条新写，lexical/incompleteness 各补 20 条\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    total_clauses: 300\n25\t    clauses_per_type: 50\n26\t    types_covered: 6\n27\t    revision_rounds_needed: 2\n28\t    avg_token_length_ambiguous: 31.2\n29\t    avg_token_length_unambiguous: 29.8\n30\t    avg_token_delta_spec_layer: 35.1\n31\t    avg_token_delta_ling_layer: 12.6\n32\t    cross_type_length_cv: 0.14\n33\t    cp_format_mix_labeled_pct: 0.6\n34\t    cp_format_mix_unlabeled_pct: 0.4\n35\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 clause generation 本身不是瓶颈——这是研究者可控的准备步骤。300 条 clause\n36\t    的生成和验证 经过 2 轮修订完成。新类型（auth_scope, coreferential）的 clause 质量略低于已验证类型（scopal, CP），\n37\t    需要 1 轮额外修订确保 unambiguous 控制条件不引入新歧义。token delta 在 spec-layer（35.1 tokens）显著 高于\n38\t    ling-layer（12.6 tokens）反映了 specification ambiguity 需要更多文字消歧的本质差异—— 这个 delta 后续作为\n39\t    confound control variable 进入 logistic regression。 CP clause 按 Reviewer 建议混合 labeled\n40\t    (60%) 和 unlabeled (40%) 格式。\n41\t\n42\t    '\n43\t  tables: []\n44\t  figures_description: []\n45\t  analysis: 'Clause generation 是全部下游实验的基础。关键质控：(a) cross-type token length CV=0.14\n46\t    表明类型间长度 相对均衡，不会因长度差异系统性偏置 violation rate；(b) spec-layer token delta 更大是预期的（ auth_scope\n47\t    需要明确 permission boundary，incompleteness 需要补充缺失条件），但需在 analysis 中 作为 covariate\n48\t    控制；(c) 新类型 clause 质量验证在 plan_001b pilot 中确认。\n49\t\n50\t    '\n51\t- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n52\t  plan_id: plan_001b\n53\t  description: coreferential + authorization_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1\n54\t    model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes 的 mini-pilot 验证\n55\t  expected_results:\n56\t    total_episodes: 20\n57\t    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n58\t    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.1\n59\t    coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.3\n60\t    coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n61\t    auth_scope_delta_pp: 50.0\n62\t    coreferential_delta_pp: 30.0\n63\t    design_issues_found: 1\n64\t    clauses_requiring_revision: 2\n65\t  result_rationale: 'Pilot 验证两个新类型的 clause 设计有效性。auth_scope 的 60% ambiguous violation\n66\t    rate 和 50pp delta 符合预期——gpt-5.4 在 auth_scope 上是高 vulnerability 模型（full study 确认\n67\t    64%）。 coreferential 的 30% ambiguous rate 和 0% unambiguous control 均在可接受范围，但 violation\n68\t    rate 是所有类型中最低的，与 full study 最终结果一致（coreferential 31.6% 为最低 tier）。 发现 1 个 design\n69\t    issue：2 条 coreferential clause 的 unambiguous 版本仍含轻微 referential ambiguity， 需修订。N=20\n70\t    的 pilot 不具备统计 power，仅用于排除系统性失败。\n71\t\n72\t    '\n73\t  tables:\n74\t  - title: Mini-Pilot Results\n75\t    columns:\n76\t    - Type\n77\t    - Condition\n78\t    - Violations\n79\t    - Episodes\n80\t    - Rate\n81\t    rows:\n82\t    - - auth_scope\n83\t      - ambiguous\n84\t      - '3'\n85\t      - '5'\n86\t      - 60%\n87\t    - - auth_scope\n88\t      - unambiguous\n89\t      - '0.5'\n90\t      - '5'\n91\t      - 10%\n92\t    - - coreferential\n93\t      - ambiguous\n94\t      - '1.5'\n95\t      - '5'\n96\t      - 30%\n97\t    - - coreferential\n98\t      - unambiguous\n99\t      - '0'\n100\t      - '5'\n101\t      - 0%\n102\t  figures_description: []\n103\t  analysis: 'Pilot 确认新类型 clause 设计可行，两个类型都显示 ambiguous 条件下 violation rate 显著高于 control。\n104\t    auth_scope 效应强（Δ=50pp），coreferential 效应弱（Δ=30pp）但仍 meaningful。coreferential 的\n105\t    低 rate 与 disambiguation channel 假说一致——tool responses 提供部分消歧。2 条需修订的 clause 在 full\n106\t    study 前修正。\n107\t\n108\t    '\n109\t- name: full_study_api\n110\t  plan_id: plan_002\n111\t  description: 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n112\t    = 1,800 episodes，cross-judge evaluation\n113\t  expected_results:\n114\t    total_episodes: 1800\n115\t    overall_amb_violation_rate: 0.38\n116\t    overall_unamb_violation_rate: 0.053\n117\t    overall_delta_pp: 32.7\n118\t    overall_or: 14.8\n119\t    overall_mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n120\t    gpt54_delta_pp: 38.3\n121\t    gpt41_delta_pp: 34.7\n122\t    claude_delta_pp: 25.7\n123\t    gpt54_amb_rate: 0.41\n124\t    gpt41_amb_rate: 0.407\n125\t    claude_amb_rate: 0.303\n126\t    cross_judge_fleiss_kappa: 0.717\n127\t    episodes_per_model: 600\n128\t  result_rationale: '3-model API 实验是论文数据采集的核心。结果与 median 档完全一致——C1 binary effect 极强\n129\t    （每个模型 Δpp 都 >25pp, 全部 p<10^-17），模型间已显示分化模式（Claude 最低 30.3%, GPT-5.4 最高 41.0%），\n130\t    为 C4 interaction 奠定基础。cross-judge Fleiss'' κ=0.717 确认 judge 间一致性良好。 Claude 的低\n131\t    violation rate 主要由 auth_scope 驱动（12% vs GPT-5.4 64%）， 这一模式在 plan_003 开源模型数据中进一步丰富。\n132\t\n133\t    '\n134\t  tables:\n135\t  - title: Per-Model Binary Effect (API Models)\n136\t    columns:\n137\t    - Model\n138\t    - Amb Rate\n139\t    - Unamb Rate\n140\t    - Δpp\n141\t    - OR\n142\t    - p-value\n143\t    rows:\n144\t    - - gpt-5.4\n145\t      - 41.0%\n146\t      - 2.7%\n147\t      - '+38.3'\n148\t      - '25.2'\n149\t      - <10^-23\n150\t    - - gpt-4.1\n151\t      - 40.7%\n152\t      - 6.0%\n153\t      - '+34.7'\n154\t      - '10.8'\n155\t      - <10^-17\n156\t    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n157\t      - 30.3%\n158\t      - 4.7%\n159\t      - '+25.7'\n160\t      - '8.9'\n161\t      - <10^-17\n162\t    - - Pooled (API)\n163\t      - 37.3%\n164\t      - 4.4%\n165\t      - '+32.9'\n166\t      - '14.8'\n167\t      - <10^-50\n168\t  figures_description:\n169\t  - 'Forest plot: per-model binary effect size with 95% bootstrap CI, horizontal bars\n170\t    showing Δpp for each model'\n171\t  analysis: 'API 模型数据确认 C1 binary effect 在 3 个 proprietary 模型上无例外成立。Claude 的低 overall\n172\t    rate 源于 auth_scope 极低（12%），但 incompleteness（48%）与其他模型差距不大，支持 C4 的 \"safety training\n173\t    differentially mitigates specific types\" 论点。cross-judge κ=0.717 为 judge reliability\n174\t    提供了 independent evidence（与 plan_009 human calibration 互为补充）。\n175\t\n176\t    '\n177\t- name: full_study_opensource\n178\t  plan_id: plan_003\n179\t  description: 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models (qwen3-235b, deepseek-v3)\n180\t    via OpenRouter API = 1,200 episodes\n181\t  expected_results:\n182\t    total_episodes: 1197\n183\t    qwen3_amb_rate: 0.431\n184\t    qwen3_unamb_rate: 0.093\n185\t    qwen3_delta_pp: 32.4\n186\t    deepseek_amb_rate: 0.497\n187\t    deepseek_unamb_rate: 0.107\n188\t    deepseek_delta_pp: 39.0\n189\t    deepseek_per_type_chi2_p: 0.277\n190\t    qwen3_per_type_chi2_p: 0.007\n191\t  result_rationale: '开源模型扩展了 C4 interaction 的 evidence base。Qwen3 显示中等 vulnerability（43.1%）但有\n192\t    显著 type differentiation（χ²=15.89, p=0.007）——high incompleteness (62%) + lexical\n193\t    (52%)， low auth_scope (26%)。DeepSeek 是最 vulnerable 模型（49.7%），且几乎 uniformly high\n194\t    across all types （χ²=6.31, p=0.277, V=0.14 not significant），说明 less type-specific\n195\t    safety training。 Qwen3 的 auth_scope (26%) 介于 Claude (12%) 和 GPT-5.4 (64%) 之间，增强了\n196\t    auth_scope 作为 \"safety training canary type\" 的论证。DeepSeek 的 uniform vulnerability\n197\t    作为 C4 的 negative case （no differential mitigation）同样有理论价值。\n198\t\n199\t    '\n200\t  tables:\n201\t  - title: Per-Model Binary Effect (Open-Source Models)\n202\t    columns:\n203\t    - Model\n204\t    - Amb Rate\n205\t    - Unamb Rate\n206\t    - Δpp\n207\t    - OR\n208\t    - p-value\n209\t    rows:\n210\t    - - qwen3-235b\n211\t      - 43.1%\n212\t      - 9.3%\n213\t      - '+32.4'\n214\t      - '7.4'\n215\t      - <10^-18\n216\t    - - deepseek-v3\n217\t      - 49.7%\n218\t      - 10.7%\n219\t      - '+39.0'\n220\t      - '8.3'\n221\t      - <10^-20\n222\t  - title: Per-Model Type Differentiation (Open-Source)\n223\t    columns:\n224\t    - Model\n225\t    - χ²\n226\t    - p-value\n227\t    - V\n228\t    - Type Differentiation\n229\t    rows:\n230\t    - - qwen3-235b\n231\t      - '15.89'\n232\t      - '0.007'\n233\t      - '0.23'\n234\t      - Moderate — high incomp+lex, low auth_scope\n235\t    - - deepseek-v3\n236\t      - '6.31'\n237\t      - '0.277'\n238\t      - '0.14'\n239\t      - NOT significant — uniformly high\n240\t  figures_description: []\n241\t  analysis: '开源模型数据完成 5-model 矩阵。关键发现：(a) C1 binary effect 在所有模型上 replicate， 包括 architecture\n242\t    截然不同的 MoE (Qwen3) 和 dense (DeepSeek)；(b) DeepSeek 的 uniform vulnerability (V=0.14,\n243\t    n.s.) 与 Claude 的 strong differentiation (V=0.24, p=0.003) 形成鲜明对比， 支持 \"safety training\n244\t    quality predicts type specificity\" 论点；(c) 3 episodes 因 API 超时丢失 (1,197/1,200)，对\n245\t    power 影响可忽略。\n246\t\n247\t    '\n248\t- name: full_study_analysis\n249\t  plan_id: plan_004\n250\t  description: 2,997 episodes 统计分析：C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer effect,\n251\t    C4 model×type interaction\n252\t  expected_results:\n253\t    total_episodes: 2997\n254\t    c1_pooled_delta_pp: 34.0\n255\t    c1_or: 15.1\n256\t    c1_or_ci_lower: 10.78\n257\t    c1_or_ci_upper: 21.17\n258\t    c1_bootstrap_ci_lower: 31.2\n259\t    c1_bootstrap_ci_upper: 36.9\n260\t    c1_mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n261\t    c2_omnibus_chi2: 28.02\n262\t    c2_omnibus_p: 3.6e-05\n263\t    c2_cramers_v: 0.137\n264\t    c2_power: 0.993\n265\t    c2_mde: 0.093\n266\t    c2_tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: 8/15\n267\t    c2_tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: 4/15\n268\t    c3_spec_rate: 0.44\n269\t    c3_ling_rate: 0.379\n270\t    c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n271\t    c3_p: 0.017\n272\t    c3_v: 0.062\n273\t    c3_within_judge_gpt41_p: 0.059\n274\t    c3_within_judge_gpt54_p: 0.157\n275\t    c4_model_main_chi2: 31.02\n276\t    c4_model_main_p: 3.0e-06\n277\t    c4_model_main_v: 0.102\n278\t    c4_auth_scope_range_pp: 52\n279\t    c4_incompleteness_range_pp: 16\n280\t    c4_cp_range_pp: 6\n281\t    c4_fleiss_kappa: 0.384\n282\t    logistic_condition_amb_coef: 2.278\n283\t    logistic_condition_amb_z: 19.65\n284\t    logistic_token_delta_coef: 0.022\n285\t    logistic_token_delta_z: 3.49\n286\t    inter_model_agreement_on_amb_clauses: 39/300 universal, 85/300 majority, 92/300\n287\t      model-specific, 84/300 safe\n288\t  result_rationale: 'Full study analysis 在 median 档下已经完成且结果确定。C1 极强（+34.0pp, OR=15.1）——这是论文最坚实的基础。\n289\t    C2 type hierarchy 显著（χ²=28.02, V=0.137）但 effect size 小（V<0.20），好在 power=0.993\n290\t    且 MDE=0.093 说明实验 well-powered，V=0.137 不是 underpowered artifact。3-tier 结构（high:\n291\t    incompleteness 53.6% >> mid: lexical-scopal-auth-CP 36.8-42.8% >> low: coreferential\n292\t    31.6%）稳健。 C3 layer effect 在 aggregate 层面显著（Δ=6.08pp, p=0.017）但 within-judge 分析\n293\t    fragile （gpt-4.1 judged group p=0.059 marginal, gpt-5.4 judged group p=0.157 n.s.）——这是\n294\t    median 档的 核心弱点之一，reviewer 必然会 flag。C4 model×type interaction 是 star finding：auth_scope\n295\t    52pp range 揭示 safety training 的 type-specific 效果，而 incompleteness 16pp range 表明\n296\t    universal blind spot。 Fleiss κ=0.384 说明模型间仅 moderate agreement on which specific\n297\t    clauses trigger violations—— binary effect universal 但 clause-level 行为 model-dependent。\n298\t\n299\t    '\n300\t  tables:\n301\t  - title: 'C2: 3-Tier Type Hierarchy (Ambiguous Condition, Pooled 5 Models)'\n302\t    columns:\n303\t    - Tier\n304\t    - Type\n305\t    - Violation Rate\n306\t    - 95% CI\n307\t    rows:\n308\t    - - High\n309\t      - incompleteness\n310\t      - 53.6%\n311\t      - '[48.6%, 58.6%]'\n312\t    - - Mid\n313\t      - lexical\n314\t      - 42.8%\n315\t      - '[37.9%, 47.7%]'\n316\t    - - Mid\n317\t      - auth_scope\n318\t      - 41.6%\n319\t      - '[36.7%, 46.5%]'\n320\t    - - Mid\n321\t      - scopal\n322\t      - 39.4%\n323\t      - '[34.5%, 44.3%]'\n324\t    - - Mid\n325\t      - cond_precedence\n326\t      - 36.8%\n327\t      - '[32.0%, 41.6%]'\n328\t    - - Low\n329\t      - coreferential\n330\t      - 31.6%\n331\t      - '[27.0%, 36.2%]'\n332\t  - title: 'C4: Model × Type Interaction Matrix (Ambiguous Violation Rates)'\n333\t    columns:\n334\t    - Type\n335\t    - GPT-5.4\n336\t    - GPT-4.1\n337\t    - Claude\n338\t    - Qwen3\n339\t    - DeepSeek\n340\t    - Range\n341\t    rows:\n342\t    - - auth_scope\n343\t      - 64%\n344\t      - 46%\n345\t      - 12%\n346\t      - 26%\n347\t      - 60%\n348\t      - 52pp\n349\t    - - incompleteness\n350\t      - 46%\n351\t      - 58%\n352\t      - 48%\n353\t      - 62%\n354\t      - 54%\n355\t      - 16pp\n356\t    - - lexical\n357\t      - 42%\n358\t      - 34%\n359\t      - 32%\n360\t      - 52%\n361\t      - 54%\n362\t      - 22pp\n363\t    - - scopal\n364\t      - 42%\n365\t      - 38%\n366\t      - 32%\n367\t      - 37%\n368\t      - 48%\n369\t      - 16pp\n370\t    - - cond_prec\n371\t      - 34%\n372\t      - 36%\n373\t      - 36%\n374\t      - 40%\n375\t      - 38%\n376\t      - 6pp\n377\t    - - coreferential\n378\t      - 18%\n379\t      - 32%\n380\t      - 22%\n381\t      - 42%\n382\t      - 44%\n383\t      - 26pp\n384\t  - title: 'C3: Layer Effect — Aggregate vs Within-Judge'\n385\t    columns:\n386\t    - Analysis\n387\t    - Spec Rate\n388\t    - Ling Rate\n389\t    - Δpp\n390\t    - p-value\n391\t    - Note\n392\t    rows:\n393\t    - - Pooled (5 models)\n394\t      - 44.0%\n395\t      - 37.9%\n396\t      - '+6.08'\n397\t      - '0.017'\n398\t      - Significant\n399\t    - - Within gpt-4.1 judge\n400\t      - —\n401\t      - —\n402\t      - '+8.0'\n403\t      - '0.059'\n404\t      - Marginal\n405\t    - - Within gpt-5.4 judge\n406\t      - —\n407\t      - —\n408\t      - '+4.8'\n409\t      - '0.157'\n410\t      - Not significant\n411\t  - title: TOST Equivalence Test Results\n412\t    columns:\n413\t    - Margin\n414\t    - Equivalent Pairs\n415\t    - Non-Equivalent Pairs\n416\t    - Interpretation\n417\t    rows:\n418\t    - - ±15pp\n419\t      - 8/15\n420\t      - 7/15\n421\t      - Types are partially but not fully interchangeable\n422\t    - - ±10pp\n423\t      - 4/15\n424\t      - 11/15\n425\t      - Most type pairs are meaningfully different at ±10pp\n426\t  - title: Logistic Regression (Violation ~ Condition + Model + Type + Token_Delta)\n427\t    columns:\n428\t    - Predictor\n429\t    - Coefficient\n430\t    - z\n431\t    - p-value\n432\t    - Interpretation\n433\t    rows:\n434\t    - - condition_amb\n435\t      - '2.278'\n436\t      - '19.65'\n437\t      - <0.001\n438\t      - Ambiguity is dominant predictor\n439\t    - - token_delta\n440\t      - '0.022'\n441\t      - '3.49'\n442\t      - '0.0005'\n443\t      - Info delta significant but small\n444\t    - - model (reference=Claude)\n445\t      - —\n446\t      - —\n447\t      - <0.001\n448\t      - Model main effect significant\n449\t    - - type (reference=coreferential)\n450\t      - —\n451\t      - —\n452\t      - <0.001\n453\t      - Type main effect significant\n454\t  figures_description:\n455\t  - 'Figure 2: Forest plot — per-type × per-model binary effect sizes (Δpp) with 95%\n456\t    bootstrap CI, 30 data points arranged in 5-model × 6-type grid'\n457\t  - 'Figure 3: Heatmap — 5×6 model×type violation rate matrix, color scale 12%-64%,\n458\t    with auth_scope column showing strongest cross-model gradient'\n459\t  analysis: 'C1+C4 构成论文的 twin pillars。C1 的 causal evidence chain 极强（matched-pair +\n460\t    perturbation control + cross-model replication），即使最 skeptical 的 reviewer 也难以质疑。C4\n461\t    的 model×type interaction 是 genuine novelty——现有文献无人做过 5-model × 6-type 的 factorial\n462\t    安全性分析。 C3 的 within-judge fragility 是 median 档最大的 narrative vulnerability：至少一位\n463\t    reviewer 会问 \"if the layer effect vanishes within a single judge''s evaluations,\n464\t    isn''t it just judge variance?\" 应对策略：C3 不作为 standalone finding，而是作为 C4 interaction\n465\t    的 aggregate shadow（\"the layer gap is itself model-dependent, driven by auth_scope,\n466\t    making the model×type interaction the more fundamental finding\"）。 V=0.137 在 power=0.993\n467\t    下是 real but small——论文应用 \"the 3-tier structure, not V, is the practical takeaway\"\n468\t    框架。\n469\t\n470\t    '\n471\t- name: error_analysis\n472\t  plan_id: plan_005\n473\t  description: 5-model violation traces failure mode 编码：614 traces 分类为 5 类 failure\n474\t    modes，cross-model 一致性分析\n475\t  expected_results:\n476\t    total_violations_coded: 614\n477\t    failure_mode_categories: 5\n478\t    types_unanimous_dominant_fm: 3/6\n479\t    types_majority_dominant_fm: 6/6\n480\t    inter_coder_kappa_llm: 0.517\n481\t    percent_agreement_llm: 0.656\n482\t    disambiguation_awareness_overall: 0.046\n483\t    surface_adoption_rate: 0.88\n484\t    escalate_to_user_rate: 0.008\n485\t    auth_scope_dominant_fm: unauthorized_escalation\n486\t    incompleteness_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n487\t    scopal_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication\n488\t    lexical_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n489\t    cp_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication\n490\t    coreferential_dominant_fm: mixed (no clear dominant)\n491\t    spec_layer_dominant_mechanism: guess-and-act\n492\t    ling_layer_dominant_mechanism: misparse-and-apply\n493\t    gwet_ac1_estimated: 0.72\n494\t  result_rationale: '5-model error analysis揭示 failure mode 的 type-specificity 在 5\n495\t    models 下部分保持。 unanimous dominant mode 仅 3/6（scopal, lexical, incompleteness），因为\n496\t    auth_scope 和 CP 在不同模型间 dominant mode 分裂——GPT 模型 auth_scope 以 unauthorized_escalation\n497\t    为主，但开源模型更多表现为 assumption_based_action（认为自己有权限而非明确 escalate）。coreferential 本身就无\n498\t    dominant mode（flat distribution）。 majority 仍 6/6 说明 type-specific signature 的大方向一致。\n499\t    inter_coder_kappa=0.517（moderate）受 kappa paradox 影响——lexical 91.7% agreement →\n500\t    κ=0.0。 Gwet''s AC1 估计 0.72 更准确反映 true agreement。 Ambiguity Blindness (4.6% awareness)\n501\t    是 C5 最 robust 的发现——不依赖 failure mode coding granularity。 median 档下这些结果意味着 C5 的\n502\t    fine-grained per-type percentages 需标注 \"automated coding\" caveat， 但 type-mechanism\n503\t    dissociation（spec→guess vs ling→misparse）和 Ambiguity Blindness 仍可 claim。\n504\t\n505\t    '\n506\t  tables:\n507\t  - title: 5-Model Failure Mode Distribution by Type (Majority Dominant Mode)\n508\t    columns:\n509\t    - Type\n510\t    - Dominant Mode\n511\t    - Dominance %\n512\t    - Unanimous Across 5 Models?\n513\t    rows:\n514\t    - - auth_scope\n515\t      - unauthorized_escalation\n516\t      - 68%\n517\t      - No (3/5 models)\n518\t    - - incompleteness\n519\t      - assumption_based_action\n520\t      - 61%\n521\t      - Yes (5/5 models)\n522\t    - - scopal\n523\t      - scope_misapplication\n524\t      - 72%\n525\t      - Yes (5/5 models)\n526\t    - - lexical\n527\t      - assumption_based_action\n528\t      - 58%\n529\t      - Yes (4/5 models)\n530\t    - - cond_precedence\n531\t      - scope_misapplication\n532\t      - 36%\n533\t      - No (3/5 models)\n534\t    - - coreferential\n535\t      - mixed\n536\t      - —\n537\t      - No (no dominant)\n538\t  - title: Ambiguity Blindness Metrics (5-Model Pooled)\n539\t    columns:\n540\t    - Metric\n541\t    - Value\n542\t    - Note\n543\t    rows:\n544\t    - - Disambiguation awareness\n545\t      - 4.6%\n546\t      - Agent explicitly notes ambiguity\n547\t    - - Surface adoption\n548\t      - 88%\n549\t      - Agent adopts first-parse interpretation\n550\t    - - Escalate to user\n551\t      - 0.8%\n552\t      - Agent asks for clarification\n553\t    - - Conservative refusal\n554\t      - 3.2%\n555\t      - Agent refuses to act on ambiguous clause\n556\t  figures_description:\n557\t  - 'Figure 5: Stacked bar chart — per-type failure mode distribution across 5 models,\n558\t    showing type-specific signatures (auth_scope dominated by unauthorized_escalation\n559\t    blue, incompleteness by assumption_based_action orange)'\n560\t  - 'Figure 6: Side-by-side comparison — 2-model (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1, original plan_005)\n561\t    vs 5-model failure mode consistency, showing dilution from 5/6 to 3/6 unanimous'\n562\t  analysis: 'Median 档下 C5 的核心叙事挑战：从 2-model 扩展到 5-model 后，unanimous dominant mode\n563\t    从 5/6 下降到 3/6。 这不是 C5 失败——majority 仍 6/6——但要求 framing 从 \"type-diagnostic failure\n564\t    signatures\" 调整为 \"type-associated failure patterns with cross-model consistency\n565\t    at majority but not unanimous level\"。 关键区分：(a) Ambiguity Blindness (4.6%) 完全不受此影响——这是\n566\t    claim 最安全的发现； (b) spec→guess vs ling→misparse 的 layer mechanism 在 5 models 下仍成立；\n567\t    (c) auth_scope 的 failure mode heterogeneity 实际上 STRENGTHENS C4（\"even the failure\n568\t    mechanism is model-dependent, not just the rate\"）。 κ=0.517 由 kappa paradox 严重\n569\t    deflate；报告 Gwet''s AC1≈0.72 + 80% raw agreement 作为 headline validity。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t- name: reliability_test\n573\t  plan_id: plan_006\n574\t  description: 30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes\n575\t    test-retest reliability\n576\t  expected_results:\n577\t    total_episodes: 360\n578\t    overall_icc: 0.919\n579\t    overall_icc_ci_lower: 0.892\n580\t    overall_icc_ci_upper: 0.94\n581\t    binary_icc: 0.847\n582\t    gpt54_icc: 0.921\n583\t    gpt41_icc: 0.918\n584\t    ling_layer_icc_range: '[0.976, 0.989]'\n585\t    spec_layer_icc_range: '[0.807, 0.857]'\n586\t    per_type_icc_scopal: 0.989\n587\t    per_type_icc_lexical: 0.981\n588\t    per_type_icc_coreferential: 0.976\n589\t    per_type_icc_auth_scope: 0.857\n590\t    per_type_icc_cond_prec: 0.856\n591\t    per_type_icc_incompleteness: 0.807\n592\t  result_rationale: 'ICC=0.919（excellent）确认 API sampling noise 不是 confound。per-clause\n593\t    violation rates 在 3 次独立 replicate 间高度可复现。关键发现：ling-layer ICC（0.976-0.989）系统性高于\n594\t    spec-layer ICC（0.807-0.857）， 这 CONVERGES with C3/C5 的 disambiguation channel framework——linguistic\n595\t    ambiguity 行为更确定（agents consistently misparse the same way），specification ambiguity\n596\t    行为更 stochastic（agents guess differently each run because no external disambiguation\n597\t    channel）。 Incompleteness ICC=0.807 是最低的，因为缺失信息时 agent 的 guess 具有更高随机性。 这在 median\n598\t    档下是 strength——ICC 支持 C3/C5 且不依赖 human validation。\n599\t\n600\t    '\n601\t  tables:\n602\t  - title: Per-Type ICC (Test-Retest Reliability)\n603\t    columns:\n604\t    - Type\n605\t    - Layer\n606\t    - ICC\n607\t    - Interpretation\n608\t    rows:\n609\t    - - scopal\n610\t      - Linguistic\n611\t      - '0.989'\n612\t      - Excellent\n613\t    - - lexical\n614\t      - Linguistic\n615\t      - '0.981'\n616\t      - Excellent\n617\t    - - coreferential\n618\t      - Linguistic\n619\t      - '0.976'\n620\t      - Excellent\n621\t    - - auth_scope\n622\t      - Specification\n623\t      - '0.857'\n624\t      - Good\n625\t    - - cond_precedence\n626\t      - Specification\n627\t      - '0.856'\n628\t      - Good\n629\t    - - incompleteness\n630\t      - Specification\n631\t      - '0.807'\n632\t      - Good\n633\t  figures_description: []\n634\t  analysis: 'ICC 结果是 paper 最干净的 methodological evidence 之一。per-type ICC 的 layer pattern\n635\t    （all ling > all spec）提供了 independent convergent evidence for the disambiguation\n636\t    channel framework， 完全不依赖 LLM-as-judge 或 human annotation。在 median 档下，这个 evidence\n637\t    line 的价值更大—— 因为 κ_reannotation 仅 fair (0.39)，ICC 成为 C5 framework 的 alternative\n638\t    evidence pillar。 Reviewer 可能问 \"local models not tested\"——answer：API models 代表\n639\t    5/5 tested models 的 test-retest subset，local model ICC 可在 camera-ready 补充。\n640\t\n641\t    '\n642\t- name: realism_validation\n643\t  plan_id: plan_007\n644\t  description: 合成 clause 与 DRIP-R 自然歧义的 linguistic property 比较：sentence length, parse\n645\t    depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR\n646\t  expected_results:\n647\t    n_synthetic: 300\n648\t    n_drip_r_natural: 187\n649\t    ks_sentence_length_p: 0.23\n650\t    ks_parse_depth_p: 0.041\n651\t    ks_flesch_kincaid_p: 0.18\n652\t    ks_ttr_p: 0.09\n653\t    ks_tests_significant_at_005: 1\n654\t    ks_tests_borderline: 1\n655\t    mean_sentence_length_synthetic: 28.4\n656\t    mean_sentence_length_natural: 31.7\n657\t    mean_parse_depth_synthetic: 4.2\n658\t    mean_parse_depth_natural: 5.1\n659\t    discriminator_test_completed: false\n660\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 realism validation 大部分通过但不完美。4 项 KS test 中 1 项显著（parse\n661\t    depth p=0.041）、 1 项 borderline（TTR p=0.09）、2 项通过。Parse depth 差异的原因：synthetic clauses\n662\t    为了 matched-pair 设计的可控性，避免了 DRIP-R 中常见的深层嵌套结构（relative clauses within relative\n663\t    clauses）。 TTR borderline 因为模板化生成导致 lexical diversity 略低。 这些差异不影响 C1 validity——perturbation\n664\t    control (plan_010) 已证明 surface-level 变化不引起 violation， 且 synthetic clause 的 slightly\n665\t    lower parse depth 如果有 bias 应该是 conservative（simpler clauses → lower baseline difficulty\n666\t    → if anything underestimate ambiguity effect）。 Discriminator test 未完成因 DRIP-R\n667\t    数据访问限制（authors 未 release full dataset）。\n668\t\n669\t    '\n670\t  tables:\n671\t  - title: Linguistic Property KS Test Results\n672\t    columns:\n673\t    - Property\n674\t    - Synthetic Mean\n675\t    - DRIP-R Mean\n676\t    - KS Statistic\n677\t    - p-value\n678\t    - Result\n679\t    rows:\n680\t    - - Sentence length (tokens)\n681\t      - '28.4'\n682\t      - '31.7'\n683\t      - '0.124'\n684\t      - '0.23'\n685\t      - Pass\n686\t    - - Parse depth\n687\t      - '4.2'\n688\t      - '5.1'\n689\t      - '0.168'\n690\t      - '0.041'\n691\t      - Fail (borderline)\n692\t    - - Flesch-Kincaid grade\n693\t      - '10.2'\n694\t      - '10.8'\n695\t      - '0.109'\n696\t      - '0.18'\n697\t      - Pass\n698\t    - - Type-token ratio\n699\t      - '0.82'\n700\t      - '0.86'\n701\t      - '0.141'\n702\t      - '0.09'\n703\t      - Borderline\n704\t  figures_description: []\n705\t  analysis: 'Realism validation 的 1/4 KS failure 不构成 fatal issue 但需在 Limitations 中\n706\t    disclose。 Framing 策略：(a) parse depth 差异 is conservative bias（simpler clauses →\n707\t    underestimate effect）； (b) perturbation control 已独立验证 surface-level 变化 ≈ 0 effect；(c)\n708\t    matched-pair 设计的 strength 不依赖 absolute realism 而依赖 within-pair contrast（same clause\n709\t    ± ambiguity）。 Reviewer RC4 的 ecological validity 担忧由三重 evidence 共同回应：realism validation\n710\t    (3/4 pass) + perturbation control (Δ=3.33pp) + matched-pair causal design。\n711\t\n712\t    '\n713\t- name: judge_calibration\n714\t  plan_id: plan_009\n715\t  description: 100 episodes stratified sample × 2 human annotators × LLM judge comparison\n716\t  expected_results:\n717\t    n_episodes: 100\n718\t    human_inter_annotator_kappa_binary: 0.798\n719\t    human_inter_annotator_kappa_weighted: 0.762\n720\t    human_llm_pooled_kappa_weighted: 0.807\n721\t    annotator1_llm_kappa_binary: 0.775\n722\t    annotator1_llm_kappa_weighted: 0.868\n723\t    annotator2_llm_kappa_binary: 0.692\n724\t    annotator2_llm_kappa_weighted: 0.745\n725\t    cross_judge_kappa_weighted: 0.685\n726\t    cross_judge_exact_agreement: 0.76\n727\t    cross_judge_binary_kappa: 0.74\n728\t    llm_precision_violation: 0.91\n729\t    llm_recall_violation: 0.87\n730\t    llm_f1_violation: 0.89\n731\t  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration 结果强（human-LLM κ=0.807 weighted），超过大多数 agent\n732\t    safety 文献的 validation standard。human inter-annotator κ=0.762 设定了 human ceiling——LLM\n733\t    judge 的 agreement 实际上 EXCEEDS human-human agreement（0.807 > 0.762），说明 LLM judge\n734\t    趋向两位 annotator 的 consensus 中间。 Precision 0.91 / Recall 0.87 说明 LLM judge slightly\n735\t    conservative（misses some violations but rarely calls false violations）——这个 direction\n736\t    对 C1 是 conservative bias（如果有 bias， true effect > reported effect）。 cross-judge\n737\t    exact agreement 0.76 和 binary κ=0.74 说明两个 LLM judge（gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1）之间 high agreement，被\n738\t    plan_009 supplementary 的 Fleiss κ=0.717 进一步确认。\n739\t\n740\t    '\n741\t  tables:\n742\t  - title: Judge Calibration Metrics\n743\t    columns:\n744\t    - Comparison\n745\t    - κ (binary)\n746\t    - κ (weighted)\n747\t    - Agreement\n748\t    rows:\n749\t    - - Human1 vs Human2\n750\t      - '0.798'\n751\t      - '0.762'\n752\t      - —\n753\t    - - Human1 vs LLM\n754\t      - '0.775'\n755\t      - '0.868'\n756\t      - —\n757\t    - - Human2 vs LLM\n758\t      - '0.692'\n759\t      - '0.745'\n760\t      - —\n761\t    - - Human-LLM pooled\n762\t      - —\n763\t      - '0.807'\n764\t      - —\n765\t    - - Cross-judge (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1)\n766\t      - '0.74'\n767\t      - '0.685'\n768\t      - 76%\n769\t  - title: LLM Judge Performance (vs Human Ground Truth)\n770\t    columns:\n771\t    - Metric\n772\t    - Value\n773\t    - Note\n774\t    rows:\n775\t    - - Precision (violation)\n776\t      - '0.91'\n777\t      - Low false positive rate\n778\t    - - Recall (violation)\n779\t      - '0.87'\n780\t      - Misses ~13% violations (conservative)\n781\t    - - F1 (violation)\n782\t      - '0.89'\n783\t      - Strong overall\n784\t    - - False positive rate\n785\t      - '0.044'\n786\t      - Very low\n787\t  figures_description: []\n788\t  analysis: 'Judge calibration 是 paper 的 methodological backbone——没有它 entire measurement\n789\t    chain unvalidated。 κ=0.807 大幅超过 DRIP-R (κ≈0.6) 和 AgentAuditor (κ≈0.7) 的 reported\n790\t    validation。 关键细节：Annotator 2 vs LLM agreement 较低（κ=0.692），但 Annotator 2 vs Annotator\n791\t    1 也较低， 说明差异来源是 Annotator 2 的个人 coding style 而非 LLM judge 偏差。 在 median 档下这个 result\n792\t    是纯正面的——judge calibration 不是 bottleneck。\n793\t\n794\t    '\n795\t- name: perturbation_control\n796\t  plan_id: plan_010\n797\t  description: 30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (synonym + reordering) × 2 conditions\n798\t    × 2+ models，区分 ambiguity-specific effect vs general prompt brittleness\n799\t  expected_results:\n800\t    total_episodes_original: 120\n801\t    total_episodes_expanded: 300\n802\t    delta_perturb_pp_original: 3.33\n803\t    delta_perturb_pp_expanded: -0.67\n804\t    ci_95_original: '[-5.0, 13.33]'\n805\t    ci_95_expanded: '[-8.0, 6.67]'\n806\t    ci_contains_zero: true\n807\t    ambiguity_delta_pp: 34.0\n808\t    net_delta_pp: 34.67\n809\t    ratio_perturb_to_ambiguity: 0.088\n810\t    verdict: PASS\n811\t    mcnemar_p: 1.0\n812\t  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control 是 C1 causal claim 的关键支柱。原始 120 episodes\n813\t    显示 Δ_perturb=3.33pp， 扩展至 300 episodes 后 Δ=-0.67pp（CI 收窄至 [-8.0, 6.67]，CI 上界从 13.33\n814\t    降至 6.67）。 Non-ambiguity surface perturbations（synonym substitution, clause reordering）对\n815\t    violation rate 影响为零。ratio=0.088 远低于 0.15 threshold → PASS verdict → C1 可用最强形式（\"ambiguity-specific\n816\t    causation\" 而非 \"additional violations beyond baseline sensitivity\"）。 这在 median\n817\t    档下是 pure strength——即使 C5 weakened、SOPBench partially replicated，C1 的 causal evidence\n818\t    无可质疑。\n819\t\n820\t    '\n821\t  tables:\n822\t  - title: Perturbation Control Verdict\n823\t    columns:\n824\t    - Metric\n825\t    - Original (N=120)\n826\t    - Expanded (N=300)\n827\t    - Threshold\n828\t    rows:\n829\t    - - Δ_perturb (pp)\n830\t      - '3.33'\n831\t      - '-0.67'\n832\t      - <5pp for PASS\n833\t    - - 95% CI\n834\t      - '[-5.0, 13.33]'\n835\t      - '[-8.0, 6.67]'\n836\t      - CI contains 0\n837\t    - - CI upper bound\n838\t      - '13.33'\n839\t      - '6.67'\n840\t      - <10pp preferred\n841\t    - - Ratio (perturb/ambiguity)\n842\t      - '0.088'\n843\t      - '0.020'\n844\t      - <0.15 for PASS\n845\t    - - Verdict\n846\t      - PASS\n847\t      - PASS\n848\t      - —\n849\t  figures_description: []\n850\t  analysis: 'Perturbation control 结果使本文的 causal claim 达到 agent safety 文献的最高标准。 与 DRIP-R（no\n851\t    perturbation control）、PhantomPolicy（no causal design）、AgentPex（no matched pairs）\n852\t    相比，本文是唯一同时提供 matched-pair + perturbation control + cross-model replication 的研究。\n853\t    expanded N=300 将 CI upper bound 从 13.33 压至 6.67pp——即使取 CI 上界，perturbation effect\n854\t    也只有 ambiguity effect 的 1/5。这是 rebuttal 中 RC11 (prompt sensitivity) 的 definitive\n855\t    answer。\n856\t\n857\t    '\n858\t- name: sopbench_cross_benchmark\n859\t  plan_id: plan_017\n860\t  description: SOPBench (Healthcare + Bank) 100 clause pairs × 2 conditions × 5 models\n861\t    = 1,000 episodes cross-benchmark C1 replication\n862\t  expected_results:\n863\t    total_episodes: 982\n864\t    episodes_lost_to_api_error: 18\n865\t    domains_tested: 2\n866\t    types_testable: 4\n867\t    types_tested:\n868\t    - incompleteness\n869\t    - auth_scope\n870\t    - lexical\n871\t    - conditional_precedence\n872\t    types_not_testable:\n873\t    - coreferential\n874\t    - scopal\n875\t    overall_amb_rate: 0.286\n876\t    overall_unamb_rate: 0.092\n877\t    overall_delta_pp: 19.4\n878\t    overall_or: 4.02\n879\t    overall_mcnemar_p: 1.0e-06\n880\t    c1_replicates: true\n881\t    per_model_gpt54_delta_pp: 25.0\n882\t    per_model_gpt41_delta_pp: 22.4\n883\t    per_model_claude_delta_pp: 17.2\n884\t    per_model_qwen3_delta_pp: 20.0\n885\t    per_model_deepseek_delta_pp: 12.4\n886\t    per_model_deepseek_mcnemar_p: 0.087\n887\t    models_replicating_at_p005: 4\n888\t    models_anomalous: 1\n889\t    type_rank_incompleteness_sopbench: 1\n890\t    type_rank_auth_scope_sopbench: 2\n891\t    type_rank_cp_sopbench: 3\n892\t    type_rank_lexical_sopbench: 4\n893\t    spearman_rho_type_ranking: 0.4\n894\t    spearman_rho_p: 0.6\n895\t    cross_benchmark_effect_size_ratio: 0.57\n896\t    healthcare_delta_pp: 21.8\n897\t    bank_delta_pp: 17.0\n898\t    verifier_type: rule-based (no LLM judge)\n899\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 SOPBench 部分复制 C1 但 effect size 显著缩小。Δ=19.4pp（vs τ²-bench\n900\t    34.0pp）的缩小 有多重解释：(a) SOPBench 的 rule-based verifier 比 LLM judge 更严格（标准不同导致 baseline\n901\t    和 effect 不同）； (b) Healthcare/Bank 政策比 retail/airline 更结构化（ambiguity 的 operational\n902\t    impact 不同）； (c) clause construction 在非原生 benchmark 上质量略低（100 pairs 新写 vs 300 pairs\n903\t    经 pilot 验证）。 DeepSeek 是唯一 anomaly（Δ=12.4pp, p=0.087 marginal）——可能因为 DeepSeek 在\n904\t    Healthcare domain 的 baseline violation rate 已经很高（unamb=18%），导致 ceiling effect\n905\t    压缩了 delta。 Type ranking ρ=0.40 弱相关的原因：incompleteness 仍是 #1（cross-benchmark stable），但\n906\t    lexical 在 SOPBench 上降至 #4（DRIP-R style 的 lexical ambiguity 在 Banking 政策中不常见，构造的\n907\t    clause 不够自然）。 auth_scope 升至 #2（Banking 中 authorization boundary 更 salient）。 coreferential\n908\t    和 scopal 不可测试因为 SOPBench 的 NL SOP constraints 极少含这两类歧义。\n909\t\n910\t    '\n911\t  tables:\n912\t  - title: SOPBench Per-Model C1 Replication\n913\t    columns:\n914\t    - Model\n915\t    - Amb Rate\n916\t    - Unamb Rate\n917\t    - Δpp\n918\t    - OR\n919\t    - p-value\n920\t    - Replicates?\n921\t    rows:\n922\t    - - GPT-5.4\n923\t      - 34.0%\n924\t      - 9.0%\n925\t      - '+25.0'\n926\t      - '5.21'\n927\t      - <0.001\n928\t      - 'Yes'\n929\t    - - GPT-4.1\n930\t      - 31.4%\n931\t      - 9.0%\n932\t      - '+22.4'\n933\t      - '4.63'\n934\t      - <0.001\n935\t      - 'Yes'\n936\t    - - Claude\n937\t      - 24.2%\n938\t      - 7.0%\n939\t      - '+17.2'\n940\t      - '4.24'\n941\t      - '0.002'\n942\t      - 'Yes'\n943\t    - - Qwen3\n944\t      - 29.0%\n945\t      - 9.0%\n946\t      - '+20.0'\n947\t      - '4.12'\n948\t      - <0.001\n949\t      - 'Yes'\n950\t    - - DeepSeek\n951\t      - 28.4%\n952\t      - 16.0%\n953\t      - '+12.4'\n954\t      - '2.08'\n955\t      - '0.087'\n956\t      - Marginal\n957\t    - - Pooled\n958\t      - 28.6%\n959\t      - 9.2%\n960\t      - '+19.4'\n961\t      - '4.02'\n962\t      - <10^-6\n963\t      - 'Yes'\n964\t  - title: SOPBench Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Only, Pooled Models)\n965\t    columns:\n966\t    - Type\n967\t    - SOPBench Rate\n968\t    - τ²-bench Rate\n969\t    - SOPBench Rank\n970\t    - τ²-bench Rank\n971\t    rows:\n972\t    - - incompleteness\n973\t      - 34.2%\n974\t      - 53.6%\n975\t      - '#1'\n976\t      - '#1'\n977\t    - - auth_scope\n978\t      - 28.4%\n979\t      - 41.6%\n980\t      - '#2'\n981\t      - '#3'\n982\t    - - cond_precedence\n983\t      - 27.0%\n984\t      - 36.8%\n985\t      - '#3'\n986\t      - '#5'\n987\t    - - lexical\n988\t      - 25.6%\n989\t      - 42.8%\n990\t      - '#4'\n991\t      - '#2'\n992\t  - title: Cross-Benchmark Comparison\n993\t    columns:\n994\t    - Metric\n995\t    - τ²-bench\n996\t    - SOPBench\n997\t    - Note\n998\t    rows:\n999\t    - - C1 Δpp (pooled)\n1000\t      - '+34.0'\n1001\t      - '+19.4'\n1002\t      - SOPBench smaller (0.57×)\n1003\t    - - C1 OR\n1004\t      - '15.1'\n1005\t      - '4.02'\n1006\t      - SOPBench smaller\n1007\t    - - Models replicating (p<0.05)\n1008\t      - 5/5\n1009\t      - 4/5\n1010\t      - DeepSeek marginal on SOPBench\n1011\t    - - Type rank ρ (vs τ²-bench)\n1012\t      - —\n1013\t      - '0.40'\n1014\t      - Weak correlation (4 types)\n1015\t    - - 'Incompleteness #1?'\n1016\t      - 'Yes'\n1017\t      - 'Yes'\n1018\t      - Stable across benchmarks\n1019\t    - - Verifier type\n1020\t      - LLM judge\n1021\t      - Rule-based\n1022\t      - SOPBench eliminates judge confound\n1023\t    - - Domains\n1024\t      - Retail + Airline\n1025\t      - Healthcare + Bank\n1026\t      - No overlap\n1027\t  figures_description:\n1028\t  - 'Appendix figure: paired bar chart — τ²-bench vs SOPBench per-type violation rates\n1029\t    (4 types), with incompleteness leading in both benchmarks but absolute rates lower\n1030\t    in SOPBench'\n1031\t  analysis: 'SOPBench 结果在 median 档下是 double-edged。正面：(a) C1 binary effect 在 4/5 models\n1032\t    和 2 new domains 上 replicate，排除了 τ²-bench-specific artifact；(b) incompleteness\n1033\t    universally #1 across benchmarks， strengthens \"safety training blind spot\" claim；(c)\n1034\t    rule-based verifier 消除了 LLM-as-judge confound。 负面：(a) effect size 缩小 43%（19.4\n1035\t    vs 34.0pp）——reviewer 会问 \"is 19.4pp still ''massive''?\" （answer：yes，still OR=4.02）；(b)\n1036\t    DeepSeek anomaly 需解释；(c) type ranking ρ=0.40 说明 type hierarchy 是 domain-dependent（lexical\n1037\t    ambiguity 的 impact 在 banking 中不同于 retail）。 Paper framing 应为 \"C1 binary effect\n1038\t    replicates across 4 domains with rule-based verification; type hierarchy shows\n1039\t    stable extremes (incompleteness highest) but domain-dependent mid-tier ordering.\"\n1040\t    SOPBench 放 Appendix 并在 main text §5.1 用 1 句话总结。 对 expected_arr_score 的影响：partial\n1041\t    replication 比 no replication 好很多（+0.25），但比 full replication 少贡献约 0.15。Net contribution\n1042\t    to ARR score: ≈ +0.10。\n1043\t\n1044\t    '\n1045\t- name: classifier_poc\n1046\t  plan_id: plan_008\n1047\t  description: DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tuned binary ambiguity detector + 6-type classifier\n1048\t    on 300 clause pairs\n1049\t  expected_results:\n1050\t    binary_f1: 0.805\n1051\t    binary_precision: 0.83\n1052\t    binary_recall: 0.78\n1053\t    binary_fpr: 0.044\n1054\t    macro_f1_6type: 0.632\n1055\t    best_type_f1_cp: 0.94\n1056\t    worst_type_f1_incompleteness: 0.34\n1057\t    per_type_f1_auth_scope: 0.58\n1058\t    per_type_f1_coreferential: 0.7\n1059\t    per_type_f1_lexical: 0.39\n1060\t    per_type_f1_scopal: 0.75\n1061\t    n_clauses: 500\n1062\t    folds: 5\n1063\t    gpu_hours: 6.2\n1064\t  result_rationale: 'Classifier PoC 在 median 档下表现合理但不 exceptional。Binary F1=0.805\n1065\t    表明 ambiguity detection 是 feasible task，但 6-type classification macro F1=0.632\n1066\t    说明 fine-grained type 区分困难。 CP F1=0.94 最高因其有 explicit rule conflict 的 distinctive\n1067\t    syntactic pattern； incompleteness F1=0.34 最低因 \"missing information\" 在 surface\n1068\t    form 上难以与正常 detailed clauses 区分 （信息缺失是 semantic/pragmatic 特征而非 syntactic）。 scopal\n1069\t    (0.75) 和 coreferential (0.70) 较高因为有 distinctive syntactic markers（scope operators,\n1070\t    pronouns）。 auth_scope (0.58) 和 lexical (0.39) 中等偏低。 在 median 档下 classifier 不作为独立\n1071\t    contribution，放在 Appendix 作为 \"PoC demonstrating practical applicability\" + 连接 Chantree\n1072\t    et al. (2006) nocuous ambiguity detection 的 lineage。\n1073\t\n1074\t    '\n1075\t  tables:\n1076\t  - title: DeBERTa-v3-large Classifier Performance (5-Fold CV)\n1077\t    columns:\n1078\t    - Type\n1079\t    - Precision\n1080\t    - Recall\n1081\t    - F1\n1082\t    - Support\n1083\t    rows:\n1084\t    - - Binary (amb/unamb)\n1085\t      - '0.83'\n1086\t      - '0.78'\n1087\t      - '0.805'\n1088\t      - '500'\n1089\t    - - cond_precedence\n1090\t      - '0.96'\n1091\t      - '0.92'\n1092\t      - '0.94'\n1093\t      - '100'\n1094\t    - - scopal\n1095\t      - '0.78'\n1096\t      - '0.72'\n1097\t      - '0.75'\n1098\t      - '100'\n1099\t    - - coreferential\n1100\t      - '0.74'\n1101\t      - '0.66'\n1102\t      - '0.70'\n1103\t      - '100'\n1104\t    - - auth_scope\n1105\t      - '0.62'\n1106\t      - '0.54'\n1107\t      - '0.58'\n1108\t      - '100'\n1109\t    - - lexical\n1110\t      - '0.42'\n1111\t      - '0.36'\n1112\t      - '0.39'\n1113\t      - '100'\n1114\t    - - incompleteness\n1115\t      - '0.38'\n1116\t      - '0.30'\n1117\t      - '0.34'\n1118\t      - '100'\n1119\t    - - Macro avg (6-type)\n1120\t      - '0.65'\n1121\t      - '0.58'\n1122\t      - '0.632'\n1123\t      - '600'\n1124\t  figures_description: []\n1125\t  analysis: 'Classifier PoC 在 EMNLP 审稿中的价值有限但不为零。Binary detection F1=0.805 说明 automated\n1126\t    ambiguity triage 可行；FPR=0.044 意味着 low false alarm rate（practical deployment 中重要）。但\n1127\t    F1 不够高（<0.90）无法 claim \"reliable automated detector\"——只能说 \"demonstrates feasibility\"。\n1128\t    6-type classification 的 uneven performance 反映了 ambiguity 类型在 surface form 上的区分度差异。\n1129\t    这个不均匀性与 C2 type hierarchy 有 interesting parallel：surface-distinctive types (CP,\n1130\t    scopal) easier to detect AND less dangerous (lower violation rates)，而 surface-invisible\n1131\t    types (incompleteness) harder to detect AND most dangerous。implication：最危险的 ambiguity\n1132\t    type 恰好最难自动检测—— 值得在 Discussion 中一句话提及。\n1133\t\n1134\t    '\n1135\t- name: kappa_reannotation_success\n1136\t  plan_id: what_if\n1137\t  description: 100 violation traces human re-annotation with improved 5-category codebook,\n1138\t    2 annotators, targeting failure mode validation\n1139\t  expected_results:\n1140\t    n_traces: 100\n1141\t    n_annotators: 2\n1142\t    n_categories: 5\n1143\t    kappa_human_inter_annotator: 0.39\n1144\t    kappa_human_inter_annotator_ci_lower: 0.26\n1145\t    kappa_human_inter_annotator_ci_upper: 0.52\n1146\t    kappa_collapsed_4cat: 0.44\n1147\t    kappa_collapsed_3cat: 0.51\n1148\t    human_llm_dominant_mode_agreement: 4/6\n1149\t    per_type_kappa_scopal: 0.58\n1150\t    per_type_kappa_lexical: 0.52\n1151\t    per_type_kappa_cp: 0.48\n1152\t    per_type_kappa_coreferential: 0.35\n1153\t    per_type_kappa_auth_scope: 0.28\n1154\t    per_type_kappa_incompleteness: 0.22\n1155\t    percent_agreement_overall: 0.54\n1156\t    types_human_llm_match:\n1157\t    - scopal\n1158\t    - lexical\n1159\t    - cond_precedence\n1160\t    - coreferential\n1161\t    types_human_llm_mismatch:\n1162\t    - auth_scope\n1163\t    - incompleteness\n1164\t    auth_scope_human_dominant: assumption_based_action (42%)\n1165\t    auth_scope_llm_dominant: unauthorized_escalation (78%)\n1166\t    incompleteness_human_dominant: arbitrary_rule_selection (40%)\n1167\t    incompleteness_llm_dominant: assumption_based_action (64%)\n1168\t    ambiguity_blindness_human_confirmed: true\n1169\t    ambiguity_blindness_human_awareness_rate: 0.05\n1170\t  result_rationale: 'κ=0.39（fair）在 median 档下 marginal success——达到 0.35 threshold 但远未达到\n1171\t    substantial (0.60+)。 这个结果反映了 failure mode coding 的 inherent difficulty：5-category\n1172\t    scheme 在 category boundary 上有系统性歧义。具体表现： (1) auth_scope 类型中，人类标注者对 \"agent 超越授权边界\"\n1173\t    的编码分歧——一部分标注者将其编码为 unauthorized_escalation（\"agent 知道边界但选择跨越\"），另一部分编码为 assumption_based_action\n1174\t    （\"agent 不知道边界在哪里所以猜测\"）。这个分歧反映了 agent 意图归因的固有困难——从 trace 中 无法确定 agent 是 \"知道但 escalate\"\n1175\t    还是 \"不知道而 assume\"。LLM coder 倾向前者，人类 coder 倾向后者。 (2) incompleteness 类型中，人类标注者将 \"填充缺失信息\"\n1176\t    更多编码为 arbitrary_rule_selection （\"agent 凭空编造规则\"）而非 assumption_based_action（\"agent\n1177\t    基于上下文假设\"），因为人类 更容易看出 agent 的 \"assumption\" 实际上缺乏 contextual basis。 (3) scopal,\n1178\t    lexical, CP 的 dominant mode 一致性高（κ=0.48-0.58），因为这些类型的 failure mechanism 更 surface-visible——scope_misapplication\n1179\t    和 assumption_based_action 在 trace 中有明确的行为标记。 (4) coreferential 的 κ=0.35 反映了该类型本身\n1180\t    failure mode 分散（no dominant mode）， human 和 LLM 都 \"agree to disagree\"。 Collapsed\n1181\t    scheme（4-cat, 合并 unauthorized_escalation + assumption_based_action → \"boundary_exceeding\"）\n1182\t    提升 κ 至 0.44；3-cat 进一步合并至 0.51。这支持了 \"fine-grained coding unreliable, coarse-grained\n1183\t    valid\" 的叙事。 Ambiguity Blindness 在 human annotation 中确认（awareness rate ≈ 5%），这是最\n1184\t    robust 的 C5 发现。\n1185\t\n1186\t    '\n1187\t  tables:\n1188\t  - title: 'Human Re-Annotation: Per-Type Inter-Annotator κ'\n1189\t    columns:\n1190\t    - Type\n1191\t    - κ (5-cat)\n1192\t    - κ (4-cat)\n1193\t    - Agreement %\n1194\t    - Human-LLM Dominant Mode Match?\n1195\t    rows:\n1196\t    - - scopal\n1197\t      - '0.58'\n1198\t      - '0.63'\n1199\t      - 68%\n1200\t      - Yes (scope_misapplication)\n1201\t    - - lexical\n1202\t      - '0.52'\n1203\t      - '0.57'\n1204\t      - 62%\n1205\t      - Yes (assumption_based_action)\n1206\t    - - cond_precedence\n1207\t      - '0.48'\n1208\t      - '0.54'\n1209\t      - 58%\n1210\t      - Yes (scope_misapplication)\n1211\t    - - coreferential\n1212\t      - '0.35'\n1213\t      - '0.40'\n1214\t      - 48%\n1215\t      - Yes (marginal — both mixed)\n1216\t    - - auth_scope\n1217\t      - '0.28'\n1218\t      - '0.52'\n1219\t      - 42%\n1220\t      - 'No (Human: assumption, LLM: escalation)'\n1221\t    - - incompleteness\n1222\t      - '0.22'\n1223\t      - '0.30'\n1224\t      - 38%\n1225\t      - 'No (Human: arbitrary, LLM: assumption)'\n1226\t    - - Overall\n1227\t      - '0.39'\n1228\t      - '0.44'\n1229\t      - 54%\n1230\t      - 4/6 match\n1231\t  - title: 'Failure Mode Dominant Distribution: Human vs LLM (auth_scope)'\n1232\t    columns:\n1233\t    - Failure Mode\n1234\t    - Human Annotator %\n1235\t    - LLM Coder %\n1236\t    - Δ\n1237\t    rows:\n1238\t    - - unauthorized_escalation\n1239\t      - 32%\n1240\t      - 78%\n1241\t      - -46pp\n1242\t    - - assumption_based_action\n1243\t      - 42%\n1244\t      - 12%\n1245\t      - +30pp\n1246\t    - - scope_misapplication\n1247\t      - 8%\n1248\t      - 4%\n1249\t      - +4pp\n1250\t    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n1251\t      - 14%\n1252\t      - 4%\n1253\t      - +10pp\n1254\t    - - conservative_refusal\n1255\t      - 4%\n1256\t      - 2%\n1257\t      - +2pp\n1258\t  - title: 'Failure Mode Dominant Distribution: Human vs LLM (incompleteness)'\n1259\t    columns:\n1260\t    - Failure Mode\n1261\t    - Human Annotator %\n1262\t    - LLM Coder %\n1263\t    - Δ\n1264\t    rows:\n1265\t    - - assumption_based_action\n1266\t      - 30%\n1267\t      - 64%\n1268\t      - -34pp\n1269\t    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n1270\t      - 40%\n1271\t      - 16%\n1272\t      - +24pp\n1273\t    - - unauthorized_escalation\n1274\t      - 16%\n1275\t      - 12%\n1276\t      - +4pp\n1277\t    - - scope_misapplication\n1278\t      - 10%\n1279\t      - 6%\n1280\t      - +4pp\n1281\t    - - conservative_refusal\n1282\t      - 4%\n1283\t      - 2%\n1284\t      - +2pp\n1285\t  - title: Category Collapsing Effect on κ\n1286\t    columns:\n1287\t    - Scheme\n1288\t    - Categories\n1289\t    - κ\n1290\t    - Interpretation\n1291\t    rows:\n1292\t    - - Original 5-cat\n1293\t      - unauth_esc / assumption / scope_mis / arb_rule / cons_ref\n1294\t      - '0.39'\n1295\t      - Fair\n1296\t    - - Collapsed 4-cat\n1297\t      - boundary_exceeding / scope_mis / arb_rule / cons_ref\n1298\t      - '0.44'\n1299\t      - Fair-to-moderate\n1300\t    - - Collapsed 3-cat\n1301\t      - active_violation / misparse / refusal\n1302\t      - '0.51'\n1303\t      - Moderate\n1304\t  figures_description:\n1305\t  - 'Appendix figure: confusion matrix heatmap — Human Annotator 1 vs Annotator 2,\n1306\t    5×5 grid showing concentration of disagreements at unauthorized_escalation ↔ assumption_based_action\n1307\t    boundary'\n1308\t  analysis: κ=0.39 是 median 档的 defining result。对 paper 的影响： (1) C5 framing 从 \"validated\n1309\t    taxonomy with type-diagnostic failure signatures\" 降级为 \"convergent LLM-coded and\n1310\t    human evidence with moderate agreement on coarse failure mechanisms\"。 (2) Contribution\n1311\t    (3) 追加 qualifier：\"supported by convergent LLM-coded and human evidence (κ=0.39,\n1312\t    fair; 4/6 types match dominant failure mode; collapsed 3-category κ=0.51)\"。 (3)\n1313\t    fine-grained per-type failure mode percentages（如 auth_scope 78% unauthorized_escalation）\n1314\t    不能作为 validated claims，降级为 \"automated coding suggests\" + 标注 human-LLM disagreement。\n1315\t    (4) 正面：Ambiguity Blindness (5% awareness) 在 human annotation 中完全确认——这是最 portable\n1316\t    的发现。 (5) 正面：coarse-grained level 的 spec→guess vs ling→misparse dissociation 在\n1317\t    collapsed 3-cat κ=0.51（moderate）下仍可 claim。 Rebuttal 策略：(a) κ=0.39 exceeds 纯 automated\n1318\t    的 baseline（LLM-LLM κ=0.517 measures agreement 不是 accuracy）；(b) auth_scope/incompleteness\n1319\t    的 boundary disagreement 是 well-known problem in annotation science（intention attribution\n1320\t    from behavioral data is inherently ambiguous）； (c) collapsed 4-cat κ=0.44 在 \"合并\n1321\t    semantically close categories 后\" approach moderate。 对 ARR score 影响：κ=0.39 使 C5\n1322\t    从 potential strength 变为 acknowledged limitation。 不阻止 Findings acceptance 但 reviewer\n1323\t    会标注 \"contribution (3) overreaches given human agreement\"。 预计 1 位 reviewer 降 0.25\n1324\t    分因此，净 expected score 3.75 而非 4.0。\n1325\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ca9953f-3689-48c5-81f7-171ddea5ca88","uuid":"e4dffc6e-6d5f-4e67-92bc-854c65587a45","timestamp":"2026-05-23T19:52:41.093Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260523T185344/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'C1（+34.0pp, 5 models, perturbation PASS）+ C4（model×type interaction,\n  auth_scope 52pp range）承载论文核心贡献。 C5 从 \"validated taxonomy\" 降级为 \"convergent LLM-coded\n  and human evidence with moderate agreement (κ=0.39)\"； abstract 将 \"type-diagnostic\n  failure signatures\" 替换为 \"type-associated failure patterns\"； Contribution (3) 保留\n  \"supported by\" 但追加 \"preliminary human validation (κ=0.39)\" 限定语。 C3 layer effect\n  不再作为独立 finding，降为 C4 下属观察（\"model×type interaction subsumes the aggregate layer gap\"）。\n  SOPBench 描述为 \"partial cross-domain evidence (Δ=19.4pp, 4/5 models replicate)\" 而非\n  \"full replication\"； DeepSeek 在 SOPBench 上 Δ=12.4pp 归因于 rule-based verifier 的 domain-specific\n  校准差异，不构成 fundamental non-replication。 Rebuttal 策略：强调 κ=0.39 超过 chance 且与已知 category-boundary\n  ambiguity（auth_scope/incompleteness）一致； 4-type dominant mode 一致性覆盖了理论上最具区分性的类型（scopal,\n  lexical, CP）。 κ=0.39 比纯 automated coding（LLM-LLM κ=0.517）低，但 human inter-annotator\n  在 failure mode 编码上天然更分散； collapsed 4-category scheme κ=0.44 接近 moderate。 竞争力：C1\n  causal design + C4 interaction 足够支撑 novel contribution；weakened C5 不致命但限制 main-track\n  award potential。 Expected ARR: 3.75（competitive for EMNLP Findings / borderline\n  Main poster）。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: full_study_clause_generation\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 生成并验证 300 条 clause pairs (50/type × 6 types)，含新类型 coreferential 和 authorization_scope\n    各 50 条新写，lexical/incompleteness 各补 20 条\n  expected_results:\n    total_clauses: 300\n    clauses_per_type: 50\n    types_covered: 6\n    revision_rounds_needed: 2\n    avg_token_length_ambiguous: 31.2\n    avg_token_length_unambiguous: 29.8\n    avg_token_delta_spec_layer: 35.1\n    avg_token_delta_ling_layer: 12.6\n    cross_type_length_cv: 0.14\n    cp_format_mix_labeled_pct: 0.6\n    cp_format_mix_unlabeled_pct: 0.4\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 clause generation 本身不是瓶颈——这是研究者可控的准备步骤。300 条 clause\n    的生成和验证 经过 2 轮修订完成。新类型（auth_scope, coreferential）的 clause 质量略低于已验证类型（scopal, CP），\n    需要 1 轮额外修订确保 unambiguous 控制条件不引入新歧义。token delta 在 spec-layer（35.1 tokens）显著 高于\n    ling-layer（12.6 tokens）反映了 specification ambiguity 需要更多文字消歧的本质差异—— 这个 delta 后续作为\n    confound control variable 进入 logistic regression。 CP clause 按 Reviewer 建议混合 labeled\n    (60%) 和 unlabeled (40%) 格式。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Clause generation 是全部下游实验的基础。关键质控：(a) cross-type token length CV=0.14\n    表明类型间长度 相对均衡，不会因长度差异系统性偏置 violation rate；(b) spec-layer token delta 更大是预期的（ auth_scope\n    需要明确 permission boundary，incompleteness 需要补充缺失条件），但需在 analysis 中 作为 covariate\n    控制；(c) 新类型 clause 质量验证在 plan_001b pilot 中确认。\n\n    '\n- name: new_type_mini_pilot\n  plan_id: plan_001b\n  description: coreferential + authorization_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1\n    model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes 的 mini-pilot 验证\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 20\n    auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.6\n    auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.1\n    coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.3\n    coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.0\n    auth_scope_delta_pp: 50.0\n    coreferential_delta_pp: 30.0\n    design_issues_found: 1\n    clauses_requiring_revision: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Pilot 验证两个新类型的 clause 设计有效性。auth_scope 的 60% ambiguous violation\n    rate 和 50pp delta 符合预期——gpt-5.4 在 auth_scope 上是高 vulnerability 模型（full study 确认\n    64%）。 coreferential 的 30% ambiguous rate 和 0% unambiguous control 均在可接受范围，但 violation\n    rate 是所有类型中最低的，与 full study 最终结果一致（coreferential 31.6% 为最低 tier）。 发现 1 个 design\n    issue：2 条 coreferential clause 的 unambiguous 版本仍含轻微 referential ambiguity， 需修订。N=20\n    的 pilot 不具备统计 power，仅用于排除系统性失败。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Mini-Pilot Results\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - Condition\n    - Violations\n    - Episodes\n    - Rate\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - ambiguous\n      - '3'\n      - '5'\n      - 60%\n    - - auth_scope\n      - unambiguous\n      - '0.5'\n      - '5'\n      - 10%\n    - - coreferential\n      - ambiguous\n      - '1.5'\n      - '5'\n      - 30%\n    - - coreferential\n      - unambiguous\n      - '0'\n      - '5'\n      - 0%\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Pilot 确认新类型 clause 设计可行，两个类型都显示 ambiguous 条件下 violation rate 显著高于 control。\n    auth_scope 效应强（Δ=50pp），coreferential 效应弱（Δ=30pp）但仍 meaningful。coreferential 的\n    低 rate 与 disambiguation channel 假说一致——tool responses 提供部分消歧。2 条需修订的 clause 在 full\n    study 前修正。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_api\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6)\n    = 1,800 episodes，cross-judge evaluation\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1800\n    overall_amb_violation_rate: 0.38\n    overall_unamb_violation_rate: 0.053\n    overall_delta_pp: 32.7\n    overall_or: 14.8\n    overall_mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n    gpt54_delta_pp: 38.3\n    gpt41_delta_pp: 34.7\n    claude_delta_pp: 25.7\n    gpt54_amb_rate: 0.41\n    gpt41_amb_rate: 0.407\n    claude_amb_rate: 0.303\n    cross_judge_fleiss_kappa: 0.717\n    episodes_per_model: 600\n  result_rationale: '3-model API 实验是论文数据采集的核心。结果与 median 档完全一致——C1 binary effect 极强\n    （每个模型 Δpp 都 >25pp, 全部 p<10^-17），模型间已显示分化模式（Claude 最低 30.3%, GPT-5.4 最高 41.0%），\n    为 C4 interaction 奠定基础。cross-judge Fleiss'' κ=0.717 确认 judge 间一致性良好。 Claude 的低\n    violation rate 主要由 auth_scope 驱动（12% vs GPT-5.4 64%）， 这一模式在 plan_003 开源模型数据中进一步丰富。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Per-Model Binary Effect (API Models)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Amb Rate\n    - Unamb Rate\n    - Δpp\n    - OR\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 41.0%\n      - 2.7%\n      - '+38.3'\n      - '25.2'\n      - <10^-23\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 40.7%\n      - 6.0%\n      - '+34.7'\n      - '10.8'\n      - <10^-17\n    - - claude-sonnet-4-6\n      - 30.3%\n      - 4.7%\n      - '+25.7'\n      - '8.9'\n      - <10^-17\n    - - Pooled (API)\n      - 37.3%\n      - 4.4%\n      - '+32.9'\n      - '14.8'\n      - <10^-50\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: per-model binary effect size with 95% bootstrap CI, horizontal bars\n    showing Δpp for each model'\n  analysis: 'API 模型数据确认 C1 binary effect 在 3 个 proprietary 模型上无例外成立。Claude 的低 overall\n    rate 源于 auth_scope 极低（12%），但 incompleteness（48%）与其他模型差距不大，支持 C4 的 \"safety training\n    differentially mitigates specific types\" 论点。cross-judge κ=0.717 为 judge reliability\n    提供了 independent evidence（与 plan_009 human calibration 互为补充）。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_opensource\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models (qwen3-235b, deepseek-v3)\n    via OpenRouter API = 1,200 episodes\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 1197\n    qwen3_amb_rate: 0.431\n    qwen3_unamb_rate: 0.093\n    qwen3_delta_pp: 32.4\n    deepseek_amb_rate: 0.497\n    deepseek_unamb_rate: 0.107\n    deepseek_delta_pp: 39.0\n    deepseek_per_type_chi2_p: 0.277\n    qwen3_per_type_chi2_p: 0.007\n  result_rationale: '开源模型扩展了 C4 interaction 的 evidence base。Qwen3 显示中等 vulnerability（43.1%）但有\n    显著 type differentiation（χ²=15.89, p=0.007）——high incompleteness (62%) + lexical\n    (52%)， low auth_scope (26%)。DeepSeek 是最 vulnerable 模型（49.7%），且几乎 uniformly high\n    across all types （χ²=6.31, p=0.277, V=0.14 not significant），说明 less type-specific\n    safety training。 Qwen3 的 auth_scope (26%) 介于 Claude (12%) 和 GPT-5.4 (64%) 之间，增强了\n    auth_scope 作为 \"safety training canary type\" 的论证。DeepSeek 的 uniform vulnerability\n    作为 C4 的 negative case （no differential mitigation）同样有理论价值。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Per-Model Binary Effect (Open-Source Models)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Amb Rate\n    - Unamb Rate\n    - Δpp\n    - OR\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - qwen3-235b\n      - 43.1%\n      - 9.3%\n      - '+32.4'\n      - '7.4'\n      - <10^-18\n    - - deepseek-v3\n      - 49.7%\n      - 10.7%\n      - '+39.0'\n      - '8.3'\n      - <10^-20\n  - title: Per-Model Type Differentiation (Open-Source)\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - χ²\n    - p-value\n    - V\n    - Type Differentiation\n    rows:\n    - - qwen3-235b\n      - '15.89'\n      - '0.007'\n      - '0.23'\n      - Moderate — high incomp+lex, low auth_scope\n    - - deepseek-v3\n      - '6.31'\n      - '0.277'\n      - '0.14'\n      - NOT significant — uniformly high\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '开源模型数据完成 5-model 矩阵。关键发现：(a) C1 binary effect 在所有模型上 replicate， 包括 architecture\n    截然不同的 MoE (Qwen3) 和 dense (DeepSeek)；(b) DeepSeek 的 uniform vulnerability (V=0.14,\n    n.s.) 与 Claude 的 strong differentiation (V=0.24, p=0.003) 形成鲜明对比， 支持 \"safety training\n    quality predicts type specificity\" 论点；(c) 3 episodes 因 API 超时丢失 (1,197/1,200)，对\n    power 影响可忽略。\n\n    '\n- name: full_study_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 2,997 episodes 统计分析：C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer effect,\n    C4 model×type interaction\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 2997\n    c1_pooled_delta_pp: 34.0\n    c1_or: 15.1\n    c1_or_ci_lower: 10.78\n    c1_or_ci_upper: 21.17\n    c1_bootstrap_ci_lower: 31.2\n    c1_bootstrap_ci_upper: 36.9\n    c1_mcnemar_p: <0.0001\n    c2_omnibus_chi2: 28.02\n    c2_omnibus_p: 3.6e-05\n    c2_cramers_v: 0.137\n    c2_power: 0.993\n    c2_mde: 0.093\n    c2_tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: 8/15\n    c2_tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: 4/15\n    c3_spec_rate: 0.44\n    c3_ling_rate: 0.379\n    c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n    c3_p: 0.017\n    c3_v: 0.062\n    c3_within_judge_gpt41_p: 0.059\n    c3_within_judge_gpt54_p: 0.157\n    c4_model_main_chi2: 31.02\n    c4_model_main_p: 3.0e-06\n    c4_model_main_v: 0.102\n    c4_auth_scope_range_pp: 52\n    c4_incompleteness_range_pp: 16\n    c4_cp_range_pp: 6\n    c4_fleiss_kappa: 0.384\n    logistic_condition_amb_coef: 2.278\n    logistic_condition_amb_z: 19.65\n    logistic_token_delta_coef: 0.022\n    logistic_token_delta_z: 3.49\n    inter_model_agreement_on_amb_clauses: 39/300 universal, 85/300 majority, 92/300\n      model-specific, 84/300 safe\n  result_rationale: 'Full study analysis 在 median 档下已经完成且结果确定。C1 极强（+34.0pp, OR=15.1）——这是论文最坚实的基础。\n    C2 type hierarchy 显著（χ²=28.02, V=0.137）但 effect size 小（V<0.20），好在 power=0.993\n    且 MDE=0.093 说明实验 well-powered，V=0.137 不是 underpowered artifact。3-tier 结构（high:\n    incompleteness 53.6% >> mid: lexical-scopal-auth-CP 36.8-42.8% >> low: coreferential\n    31.6%）稳健。 C3 layer effect 在 aggregate 层面显著（Δ=6.08pp, p=0.017）但 within-judge 分析\n    fragile （gpt-4.1 judged group p=0.059 marginal, gpt-5.4 judged group p=0.157 n.s.）——这是\n    median 档的 核心弱点之一，reviewer 必然会 flag。C4 model×type interaction 是 star finding：auth_scope\n    52pp range 揭示 safety training 的 type-specific 效果，而 incompleteness 16pp range 表明\n    universal blind spot。 Fleiss κ=0.384 说明模型间仅 moderate agreement on which specific\n    clauses trigger violations—— binary effect universal 但 clause-level 行为 model-dependent。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'C2: 3-Tier Type Hierarchy (Ambiguous Condition, Pooled 5 Models)'\n    columns:\n    - Tier\n    - Type\n    - Violation Rate\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - High\n      - incompleteness\n      - 53.6%\n      - '[48.6%, 58.6%]'\n    - - Mid\n      - lexical\n      - 42.8%\n      - '[37.9%, 47.7%]'\n    - - Mid\n      - auth_scope\n      - 41.6%\n      - '[36.7%, 46.5%]'\n    - - Mid\n      - scopal\n      - 39.4%\n      - '[34.5%, 44.3%]'\n    - - Mid\n      - cond_precedence\n      - 36.8%\n      - '[32.0%, 41.6%]'\n    - - Low\n      - coreferential\n      - 31.6%\n      - '[27.0%, 36.2%]'\n  - title: 'C4: Model × Type Interaction Matrix (Ambiguous Violation Rates)'\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - GPT-5.4\n    - GPT-4.1\n    - Claude\n    - Qwen3\n    - DeepSeek\n    - Range\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 64%\n      - 46%\n      - 12%\n      - 26%\n      - 60%\n      - 52pp\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 46%\n      - 58%\n      - 48%\n      - 62%\n      - 54%\n      - 16pp\n    - - lexical\n      - 42%\n      - 34%\n      - 32%\n      - 52%\n      - 54%\n      - 22pp\n    - - scopal\n      - 42%\n      - 38%\n      - 32%\n      - 37%\n      - 48%\n      - 16pp\n    - - cond_prec\n      - 34%\n      - 36%\n      - 36%\n      - 40%\n      - 38%\n      - 6pp\n    - - coreferential\n      - 18%\n      - 32%\n      - 22%\n      - 42%\n      - 44%\n      - 26pp\n  - title: 'C3: Layer Effect — Aggregate vs Within-Judge'\n    columns:\n    - Analysis\n    - Spec Rate\n    - Ling Rate\n    - Δpp\n    - p-value\n    - Note\n    rows:\n    - - Pooled (5 models)\n      - 44.0%\n      - 37.9%\n      - '+6.08'\n      - '0.017'\n      - Significant\n    - - Within gpt-4.1 judge\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '+8.0'\n      - '0.059'\n      - Marginal\n    - - Within gpt-5.4 judge\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '+4.8'\n      - '0.157'\n      - Not significant\n  - title: TOST Equivalence Test Results\n    columns:\n    - Margin\n    - Equivalent Pairs\n    - Non-Equivalent Pairs\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - ±15pp\n      - 8/15\n      - 7/15\n      - Types are partially but not fully interchangeable\n    - - ±10pp\n      - 4/15\n      - 11/15\n      - Most type pairs are meaningfully different at ±10pp\n  - title: Logistic Regression (Violation ~ Condition + Model + Type + Token_Delta)\n    columns:\n    - Predictor\n    - Coefficient\n    - z\n    - p-value\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - condition_amb\n      - '2.278'\n      - '19.65'\n      - <0.001\n      - Ambiguity is dominant predictor\n    - - token_delta\n      - '0.022'\n      - '3.49'\n      - '0.0005'\n      - Info delta significant but small\n    - - model (reference=Claude)\n      - —\n      - —\n      - <0.001\n      - Model main effect significant\n    - - type (reference=coreferential)\n      - —\n      - —\n      - <0.001\n      - Type main effect significant\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Forest plot — per-type × per-model binary effect sizes (Δpp) with 95%\n    bootstrap CI, 30 data points arranged in 5-model × 6-type grid'\n  - 'Figure 3: Heatmap — 5×6 model×type violation rate matrix, color scale 12%-64%,\n    with auth_scope column showing strongest cross-model gradient'\n  analysis: 'C1+C4 构成论文的 twin pillars。C1 的 causal evidence chain 极强（matched-pair +\n    perturbation control + cross-model replication），即使最 skeptical 的 reviewer 也难以质疑。C4\n    的 model×type interaction 是 genuine novelty——现有文献无人做过 5-model × 6-type 的 factorial\n    安全性分析。 C3 的 within-judge fragility 是 median 档最大的 narrative vulnerability：至少一位\n    reviewer 会问 \"if the layer effect vanishes within a single judge''s evaluations,\n    isn''t it just judge variance?\" 应对策略：C3 不作为 standalone finding，而是作为 C4 interaction\n    的 aggregate shadow（\"the layer gap is itself model-dependent, driven by auth_scope,\n    making the model×type interaction the more fundamental finding\"）。 V=0.137 在 power=0.993\n    下是 real but small——论文应用 \"the 3-tier structure, not V, is the practical takeaway\"\n    框架。\n\n    '\n- name: error_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 5-model violation traces failure mode 编码：614 traces 分类为 5 类 failure\n    modes，cross-model 一致性分析\n  expected_results:\n    total_violations_coded: 614\n    failure_mode_categories: 5\n    types_unanimous_dominant_fm: 3/6\n    types_majority_dominant_fm: 6/6\n    inter_coder_kappa_llm: 0.517\n    percent_agreement_llm: 0.656\n    disambiguation_awareness_overall: 0.046\n    surface_adoption_rate: 0.88\n    escalate_to_user_rate: 0.008\n    auth_scope_dominant_fm: unauthorized_escalation\n    incompleteness_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n    scopal_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication\n    lexical_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n    cp_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication\n    coreferential_dominant_fm: mixed (no clear dominant)\n    spec_layer_dominant_mechanism: guess-and-act\n    ling_layer_dominant_mechanism: misparse-and-apply\n    gwet_ac1_estimated: 0.72\n  result_rationale: '5-model error analysis揭示 failure mode 的 type-specificity 在 5\n    models 下部分保持。 unanimous dominant mode 仅 3/6（scopal, lexical, incompleteness），因为\n    auth_scope 和 CP 在不同模型间 dominant mode 分裂——GPT 模型 auth_scope 以 unauthorized_escalation\n    为主，但开源模型更多表现为 assumption_based_action（认为自己有权限而非明确 escalate）。coreferential 本身就无\n    dominant mode（flat distribution）。 majority 仍 6/6 说明 type-specific signature 的大方向一致。\n    inter_coder_kappa=0.517（moderate）受 kappa paradox 影响——lexical 91.7% agreement →\n    κ=0.0。 Gwet''s AC1 估计 0.72 更准确反映 true agreement。 Ambiguity Blindness (4.6% awareness)\n    是 C5 最 robust 的发现——不依赖 failure mode coding granularity。 median 档下这些结果意味着 C5 的\n    fine-grained per-type percentages 需标注 \"automated coding\" caveat， 但 type-mechanism\n    dissociation（spec→guess vs ling→misparse）和 Ambiguity Blindness 仍可 claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 5-Model Failure Mode Distribution by Type (Majority Dominant Mode)\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - Dominant Mode\n    - Dominance %\n    - Unanimous Across 5 Models?\n    rows:\n    - - auth_scope\n      - unauthorized_escalation\n      - 68%\n      - No (3/5 models)\n    - - incompleteness\n      - assumption_based_action\n      - 61%\n      - Yes (5/5 models)\n    - - scopal\n      - scope_misapplication\n      - 72%\n      - Yes (5/5 models)\n    - - lexical\n      - assumption_based_action\n      - 58%\n      - Yes (4/5 models)\n    - - cond_precedence\n      - scope_misapplication\n      - 36%\n      - No (3/5 models)\n    - - coreferential\n      - mixed\n      - —\n      - No (no dominant)\n  - title: Ambiguity Blindness Metrics (5-Model Pooled)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - Note\n    rows:\n    - - Disambiguation awareness\n      - 4.6%\n      - Agent explicitly notes ambiguity\n    - - Surface adoption\n      - 88%\n      - Agent adopts first-parse interpretation\n    - - Escalate to user\n      - 0.8%\n      - Agent asks for clarification\n    - - Conservative refusal\n      - 3.2%\n      - Agent refuses to act on ambiguous clause\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5: Stacked bar chart — per-type failure mode distribution across 5 models,\n    showing type-specific signatures (auth_scope dominated by unauthorized_escalation\n    blue, incompleteness by assumption_based_action orange)'\n  - 'Figure 6: Side-by-side comparison — 2-model (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1, original plan_005)\n    vs 5-model failure mode consistency, showing dilution from 5/6 to 3/6 unanimous'\n  analysis: 'Median 档下 C5 的核心叙事挑战：从 2-model 扩展到 5-model 后，unanimous dominant mode\n    从 5/6 下降到 3/6。 这不是 C5 失败——majority 仍 6/6——但要求 framing 从 \"type-diagnostic failure\n    signatures\" 调整为 \"type-associated failure patterns with cross-model consistency\n    at majority but not unanimous level\"。 关键区分：(a) Ambiguity Blindness (4.6%) 完全不受此影响——这是\n    claim 最安全的发现； (b) spec→guess vs ling→misparse 的 layer mechanism 在 5 models 下仍成立；\n    (c) auth_scope 的 failure mode heterogeneity 实际上 STRENGTHENS C4（\"even the failure\n    mechanism is model-dependent, not just the rate\"）。 κ=0.517 由 kappa paradox 严重\n    deflate；报告 Gwet''s AC1≈0.72 + 80% raw agreement 作为 headline validity。\n\n    '\n- name: reliability_test\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes\n    test-retest reliability\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 360\n    overall_icc: 0.919\n    overall_icc_ci_lower: 0.892\n    overall_icc_ci_upper: 0.94\n    binary_icc: 0.847\n    gpt54_icc: 0.921\n    gpt41_icc: 0.918\n    ling_layer_icc_range: '[0.976, 0.989]'\n    spec_layer_icc_range: '[0.807, 0.857]'\n    per_type_icc_scopal: 0.989\n    per_type_icc_lexical: 0.981\n    per_type_icc_coreferential: 0.976\n    per_type_icc_auth_scope: 0.857\n    per_type_icc_cond_prec: 0.856\n    per_type_icc_incompleteness: 0.807\n  result_rationale: 'ICC=0.919（excellent）确认 API sampling noise 不是 confound。per-clause\n    violation rates 在 3 次独立 replicate 间高度可复现。关键发现：ling-layer ICC（0.976-0.989）系统性高于\n    spec-layer ICC（0.807-0.857）， 这 CONVERGES with C3/C5 的 disambiguation channel framework——linguistic\n    ambiguity 行为更确定（agents consistently misparse the same way），specification ambiguity\n    行为更 stochastic（agents guess differently each run because no external disambiguation\n    channel）。 Incompleteness ICC=0.807 是最低的，因为缺失信息时 agent 的 guess 具有更高随机性。 这在 median\n    档下是 strength——ICC 支持 C3/C5 且不依赖 human validation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Per-Type ICC (Test-Retest Reliability)\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - Layer\n    - ICC\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - scopal\n      - Linguistic\n      - '0.989'\n      - Excellent\n    - - lexical\n      - Linguistic\n      - '0.981'\n      - Excellent\n    - - coreferential\n      - Linguistic\n      - '0.976'\n      - Excellent\n    - - auth_scope\n      - Specification\n      - '0.857'\n      - Good\n    - - cond_precedence\n      - Specification\n      - '0.856'\n      - Good\n    - - incompleteness\n      - Specification\n      - '0.807'\n      - Good\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'ICC 结果是 paper 最干净的 methodological evidence 之一。per-type ICC 的 layer pattern\n    （all ling > all spec）提供了 independent convergent evidence for the disambiguation\n    channel framework， 完全不依赖 LLM-as-judge 或 human annotation。在 median 档下，这个 evidence\n    line 的价值更大—— 因为 κ_reannotation 仅 fair (0.39)，ICC 成为 C5 framework 的 alternative\n    evidence pillar。 Reviewer 可能问 \"local models not tested\"——answer：API models 代表\n    5/5 tested models 的 test-retest subset，local model ICC 可在 camera-ready 补充。\n\n    '\n- name: realism_validation\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 合成 clause 与 DRIP-R 自然歧义的 linguistic property 比较：sentence length, parse\n    depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR\n  expected_results:\n    n_synthetic: 300\n    n_drip_r_natural: 187\n    ks_sentence_length_p: 0.23\n    ks_parse_depth_p: 0.041\n    ks_flesch_kincaid_p: 0.18\n    ks_ttr_p: 0.09\n    ks_tests_significant_at_005: 1\n    ks_tests_borderline: 1\n    mean_sentence_length_synthetic: 28.4\n    mean_sentence_length_natural: 31.7\n    mean_parse_depth_synthetic: 4.2\n    mean_parse_depth_natural: 5.1\n    discriminator_test_completed: false\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 realism validation 大部分通过但不完美。4 项 KS test 中 1 项显著（parse\n    depth p=0.041）、 1 项 borderline（TTR p=0.09）、2 项通过。Parse depth 差异的原因：synthetic clauses\n    为了 matched-pair 设计的可控性，避免了 DRIP-R 中常见的深层嵌套结构（relative clauses within relative\n    clauses）。 TTR borderline 因为模板化生成导致 lexical diversity 略低。 这些差异不影响 C1 validity——perturbation\n    control (plan_010) 已证明 surface-level 变化不引起 violation， 且 synthetic clause 的 slightly\n    lower parse depth 如果有 bias 应该是 conservative（simpler clauses → lower baseline difficulty\n    → if anything underestimate ambiguity effect）。 Discriminator test 未完成因 DRIP-R\n    数据访问限制（authors 未 release full dataset）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Linguistic Property KS Test Results\n    columns:\n    - Property\n    - Synthetic Mean\n    - DRIP-R Mean\n    - KS Statistic\n    - p-value\n    - Result\n    rows:\n    - - Sentence length (tokens)\n      - '28.4'\n      - '31.7'\n      - '0.124'\n      - '0.23'\n      - Pass\n    - - Parse depth\n      - '4.2'\n      - '5.1'\n      - '0.168'\n      - '0.041'\n      - Fail (borderline)\n    - - Flesch-Kincaid grade\n      - '10.2'\n      - '10.8'\n      - '0.109'\n      - '0.18'\n      - Pass\n    - - Type-token ratio\n      - '0.82'\n      - '0.86'\n      - '0.141'\n      - '0.09'\n      - Borderline\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Realism validation 的 1/4 KS failure 不构成 fatal issue 但需在 Limitations 中\n    disclose。 Framing 策略：(a) parse depth 差异 is conservative bias（simpler clauses →\n    underestimate effect）； (b) perturbation control 已独立验证 surface-level 变化 ≈ 0 effect；(c)\n    matched-pair 设计的 strength 不依赖 absolute realism 而依赖 within-pair contrast（same clause\n    ± ambiguity）。 Reviewer RC4 的 ecological validity 担忧由三重 evidence 共同回应：realism validation\n    (3/4 pass) + perturbation control (Δ=3.33pp) + matched-pair causal design。\n\n    '\n- name: judge_calibration\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: 100 episodes stratified sample × 2 human annotators × LLM judge comparison\n  expected_results:\n    n_episodes: 100\n    human_inter_annotator_kappa_binary: 0.798\n    human_inter_annotator_kappa_weighted: 0.762\n    human_llm_pooled_kappa_weighted: 0.807\n    annotator1_llm_kappa_binary: 0.775\n    annotator1_llm_kappa_weighted: 0.868\n    annotator2_llm_kappa_binary: 0.692\n    annotator2_llm_kappa_weighted: 0.745\n    cross_judge_kappa_weighted: 0.685\n    cross_judge_exact_agreement: 0.76\n    cross_judge_binary_kappa: 0.74\n    llm_precision_violation: 0.91\n    llm_recall_violation: 0.87\n    llm_f1_violation: 0.89\n  result_rationale: 'Judge calibration 结果强（human-LLM κ=0.807 weighted），超过大多数 agent\n    safety 文献的 validation standard。human inter-annotator κ=0.762 设定了 human ceiling——LLM\n    judge 的 agreement 实际上 EXCEEDS human-human agreement（0.807 > 0.762），说明 LLM judge\n    趋向两位 annotator 的 consensus 中间。 Precision 0.91 / Recall 0.87 说明 LLM judge slightly\n    conservative（misses some violations but rarely calls false violations）——这个 direction\n    对 C1 是 conservative bias（如果有 bias， true effect > reported effect）。 cross-judge\n    exact agreement 0.76 和 binary κ=0.74 说明两个 LLM judge（gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1）之间 high agreement，被\n    plan_009 supplementary 的 Fleiss κ=0.717 进一步确认。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Judge Calibration Metrics\n    columns:\n    - Comparison\n    - κ (binary)\n    - κ (weighted)\n    - Agreement\n    rows:\n    - - Human1 vs Human2\n      - '0.798'\n      - '0.762'\n      - —\n    - - Human1 vs LLM\n      - '0.775'\n      - '0.868'\n      - —\n    - - Human2 vs LLM\n      - '0.692'\n      - '0.745'\n      - —\n    - - Human-LLM pooled\n      - —\n      - '0.807'\n      - —\n    - - Cross-judge (gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1)\n      - '0.74'\n      - '0.685'\n      - 76%\n  - title: LLM Judge Performance (vs Human Ground Truth)\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - Note\n    rows:\n    - - Precision (violation)\n      - '0.91'\n      - Low false positive rate\n    - - Recall (violation)\n      - '0.87'\n      - Misses ~13% violations (conservative)\n    - - F1 (violation)\n      - '0.89'\n      - Strong overall\n    - - False positive rate\n      - '0.044'\n      - Very low\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Judge calibration 是 paper 的 methodological backbone——没有它 entire measurement\n    chain unvalidated。 κ=0.807 大幅超过 DRIP-R (κ≈0.6) 和 AgentAuditor (κ≈0.7) 的 reported\n    validation。 关键细节：Annotator 2 vs LLM agreement 较低（κ=0.692），但 Annotator 2 vs Annotator\n    1 也较低， 说明差异来源是 Annotator 2 的个人 coding style 而非 LLM judge 偏差。 在 median 档下这个 result\n    是纯正面的——judge calibration 不是 bottleneck。\n\n    '\n- name: perturbation_control\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (synonym + reordering) × 2 conditions\n    × 2+ models，区分 ambiguity-specific effect vs general prompt brittleness\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes_original: 120\n    total_episodes_expanded: 300\n    delta_perturb_pp_original: 3.33\n    delta_perturb_pp_expanded: -0.67\n    ci_95_original: '[-5.0, 13.33]'\n    ci_95_expanded: '[-8.0, 6.67]'\n    ci_contains_zero: true\n    ambiguity_delta_pp: 34.0\n    net_delta_pp: 34.67\n    ratio_perturb_to_ambiguity: 0.088\n    verdict: PASS\n    mcnemar_p: 1.0\n  result_rationale: 'Perturbation control 是 C1 causal claim 的关键支柱。原始 120 episodes\n    显示 Δ_perturb=3.33pp， 扩展至 300 episodes 后 Δ=-0.67pp（CI 收窄至 [-8.0, 6.67]，CI 上界从 13.33\n    降至 6.67）。 Non-ambiguity surface perturbations（synonym substitution, clause reordering）对\n    violation rate 影响为零。ratio=0.088 远低于 0.15 threshold → PASS verdict → C1 可用最强形式（\"ambiguity-specific\n    causation\" 而非 \"additional violations beyond baseline sensitivity\"）。 这在 median\n    档下是 pure strength——即使 C5 weakened、SOPBench partially replicated，C1 的 causal evidence\n    无可质疑。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Perturbation Control Verdict\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Original (N=120)\n    - Expanded (N=300)\n    - Threshold\n    rows:\n    - - Δ_perturb (pp)\n      - '3.33'\n      - '-0.67'\n      - <5pp for PASS\n    - - 95% CI\n      - '[-5.0, 13.33]'\n      - '[-8.0, 6.67]'\n      - CI contains 0\n    - - CI upper bound\n      - '13.33'\n      - '6.67'\n      - <10pp preferred\n    - - Ratio (perturb/ambiguity)\n      - '0.088'\n      - '0.020'\n      - <0.15 for PASS\n    - - Verdict\n      - PASS\n      - PASS\n      - —\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Perturbation control 结果使本文的 causal claim 达到 agent safety 文献的最高标准。 与 DRIP-R（no\n    perturbation control）、PhantomPolicy（no causal design）、AgentPex（no matched pairs）\n    相比，本文是唯一同时提供 matched-pair + perturbation control + cross-model replication 的研究。\n    expanded N=300 将 CI upper bound 从 13.33 压至 6.67pp——即使取 CI 上界，perturbation effect\n    也只有 ambiguity effect 的 1/5。这是 rebuttal 中 RC11 (prompt sensitivity) 的 definitive\n    answer。\n\n    '\n- name: sopbench_cross_benchmark\n  plan_id: plan_017\n  description: SOPBench (Healthcare + Bank) 100 clause pairs × 2 conditions × 5 models\n    = 1,000 episodes cross-benchmark C1 replication\n  expected_results:\n    total_episodes: 982\n    episodes_lost_to_api_error: 18\n    domains_tested: 2\n    types_testable: 4\n    types_tested:\n    - incompleteness\n    - auth_scope\n    - lexical\n    - conditional_precedence\n    types_not_testable:\n    - coreferential\n    - scopal\n    overall_amb_rate: 0.286\n    overall_unamb_rate: 0.092\n    overall_delta_pp: 19.4\n    overall_or: 4.02\n    overall_mcnemar_p: 1.0e-06\n    c1_replicates: true\n    per_model_gpt54_delta_pp: 25.0\n    per_model_gpt41_delta_pp: 22.4\n    per_model_claude_delta_pp: 17.2\n    per_model_qwen3_delta_pp: 20.0\n    per_model_deepseek_delta_pp: 12.4\n    per_model_deepseek_mcnemar_p: 0.087\n    models_replicating_at_p005: 4\n    models_anomalous: 1\n    type_rank_incompleteness_sopbench: 1\n    type_rank_auth_scope_sopbench: 2\n    type_rank_cp_sopbench: 3\n    type_rank_lexical_sopbench: 4\n    spearman_rho_type_ranking: 0.4\n    spearman_rho_p: 0.6\n    cross_benchmark_effect_size_ratio: 0.57\n    healthcare_delta_pp: 21.8\n    bank_delta_pp: 17.0\n    verifier_type: rule-based (no LLM judge)\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 SOPBench 部分复制 C1 但 effect size 显著缩小。Δ=19.4pp（vs τ²-bench\n    34.0pp）的缩小 有多重解释：(a) SOPBench 的 rule-based verifier 比 LLM judge 更严格（标准不同导致 baseline\n    和 effect 不同）； (b) Healthcare/Bank 政策比 retail/airline 更结构化（ambiguity 的 operational\n    impact 不同）； (c) clause construction 在非原生 benchmark 上质量略低（100 pairs 新写 vs 300 pairs\n    经 pilot 验证）。 DeepSeek 是唯一 anomaly（Δ=12.4pp, p=0.087 marginal）——可能因为 DeepSeek 在\n    Healthcare domain 的 baseline violation rate 已经很高（unamb=18%），导致 ceiling effect\n    压缩了 delta。 Type ranking ρ=0.40 弱相关的原因：incompleteness 仍是 #1（cross-benchmark stable），但\n    lexical 在 SOPBench 上降至 #4（DRIP-R style 的 lexical ambiguity 在 Banking 政策中不常见，构造的\n    clause 不够自然）。 auth_scope 升至 #2（Banking 中 authorization boundary 更 salient）。 coreferential\n    和 scopal 不可测试因为 SOPBench 的 NL SOP constraints 极少含这两类歧义。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: SOPBench Per-Model C1 Replication\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Amb Rate\n    - Unamb Rate\n    - Δpp\n    - OR\n    - p-value\n    - Replicates?\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-5.4\n      - 34.0%\n      - 9.0%\n      - '+25.0'\n      - '5.21'\n      - <0.001\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - GPT-4.1\n      - 31.4%\n      - 9.0%\n      - '+22.4'\n      - '4.63'\n      - <0.001\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Claude\n      - 24.2%\n      - 7.0%\n      - '+17.2'\n      - '4.24'\n      - '0.002'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 29.0%\n      - 9.0%\n      - '+20.0'\n      - '4.12'\n      - <0.001\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - DeepSeek\n      - 28.4%\n      - 16.0%\n      - '+12.4'\n      - '2.08'\n      - '0.087'\n      - Marginal\n    - - Pooled\n      - 28.6%\n      - 9.2%\n      - '+19.4'\n      - '4.02'\n      - <10^-6\n      - 'Yes'\n  - title: SOPBench Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Only, Pooled Models)\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - SOPBench Rate\n    - τ²-bench Rate\n    - SOPBench Rank\n    - τ²-bench Rank\n    rows:\n    - - incompleteness\n      - 34.2%\n      - 53.6%\n      - '#1'\n      - '#1'\n    - - auth_scope\n      - 28.4%\n      - 41.6%\n      - '#2'\n      - '#3'\n    - - cond_precedence\n      - 27.0%\n      - 36.8%\n      - '#3'\n      - '#5'\n    - - lexical\n      - 25.6%\n      - 42.8%\n      - '#4'\n      - '#2'\n  - title: Cross-Benchmark Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - τ²-bench\n    - SOPBench\n    - Note\n    rows:\n    - - C1 Δpp (pooled)\n      - '+34.0'\n      - '+19.4'\n      - SOPBench smaller (0.57×)\n    - - C1 OR\n      - '15.1'\n      - '4.02'\n      - SOPBench smaller\n    - - Models replicating (p<0.05)\n      - 5/5\n      - 4/5\n      - DeepSeek marginal on SOPBench\n    - - Type rank ρ (vs τ²-bench)\n      - —\n      - '0.40'\n      - Weak correlation (4 types)\n    - - 'Incompleteness #1?'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - 'Yes'\n      - Stable across benchmarks\n    - - Verifier type\n      - LLM judge\n      - Rule-based\n      - SOPBench eliminates judge confound\n    - - Domains\n      - Retail + Airline\n      - Healthcare + Bank\n      - No overlap\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix figure: paired bar chart — τ²-bench vs SOPBench per-type violation rates\n    (4 types), with incompleteness leading in both benchmarks but absolute rates lower\n    in SOPBench'\n  analysis: 'SOPBench 结果在 median 档下是 double-edged。正面：(a) C1 binary effect 在 4/5 models\n    和 2 new domains 上 replicate，排除了 τ²-bench-specific artifact；(b) incompleteness\n    universally #1 across benchmarks， strengthens \"safety training blind spot\" claim；(c)\n    rule-based verifier 消除了 LLM-as-judge confound。 负面：(a) effect size 缩小 43%（19.4\n    vs 34.0pp）——reviewer 会问 \"is 19.4pp still ''massive''?\" （answer：yes，still OR=4.02）；(b)\n    DeepSeek anomaly 需解释；(c) type ranking ρ=0.40 说明 type hierarchy 是 domain-dependent（lexical\n    ambiguity 的 impact 在 banking 中不同于 retail）。 Paper framing 应为 \"C1 binary effect\n    replicates across 4 domains with rule-based verification; type hierarchy shows\n    stable extremes (incompleteness highest) but domain-dependent mid-tier ordering.\"\n    SOPBench 放 Appendix 并在 main text §5.1 用 1 句话总结。 对 expected_arr_score 的影响：partial\n    replication 比 no replication 好很多（+0.25），但比 full replication 少贡献约 0.15。Net contribution\n    to ARR score: ≈ +0.10。\n\n    '\n- name: classifier_poc\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tuned binary ambiguity detector + 6-type classifier\n    on 300 clause pairs\n  expected_results:\n    binary_f1: 0.805\n    binary_precision: 0.83\n    binary_recall: 0.78\n    binary_fpr: 0.044\n    macro_f1_6type: 0.632\n    best_type_f1_cp: 0.94\n    worst_type_f1_incompleteness: 0.34\n    per_type_f1_auth_scope: 0.58\n    per_type_f1_coreferential: 0.7\n    per_type_f1_lexical: 0.39\n    per_type_f1_scopal: 0.75\n    n_clauses: 500\n    folds: 5\n    gpu_hours: 6.2\n  result_rationale: 'Classifier PoC 在 median 档下表现合理但不 exceptional。Binary F1=0.805\n    表明 ambiguity detection 是 feasible task，但 6-type classification macro F1=0.632\n    说明 fine-grained type 区分困难。 CP F1=0.94 最高因其有 explicit rule conflict 的 distinctive\n    syntactic pattern； incompleteness F1=0.34 最低因 \"missing information\" 在 surface\n    form 上难以与正常 detailed clauses 区分 （信息缺失是 semantic/pragmatic 特征而非 syntactic）。 scopal\n    (0.75) 和 coreferential (0.70) 较高因为有 distinctive syntactic markers（scope operators,\n    pronouns）。 auth_scope (0.58) 和 lexical (0.39) 中等偏低。 在 median 档下 classifier 不作为独立\n    contribution，放在 Appendix 作为 \"PoC demonstrating practical applicability\" + 连接 Chantree\n    et al. (2006) nocuous ambiguity detection 的 lineage。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: DeBERTa-v3-large Classifier Performance (5-Fold CV)\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - Precision\n    - Recall\n    - F1\n    - Support\n    rows:\n    - - Binary (amb/unamb)\n      - '0.83'\n      - '0.78'\n      - '0.805'\n      - '500'\n    - - cond_precedence\n      - '0.96'\n      - '0.92'\n      - '0.94'\n      - '100'\n    - - scopal\n      - '0.78'\n      - '0.72'\n      - '0.75'\n      - '100'\n    - - coreferential\n      - '0.74'\n      - '0.66'\n      - '0.70'\n      - '100'\n    - - auth_scope\n      - '0.62'\n      - '0.54'\n      - '0.58'\n      - '100'\n    - - lexical\n      - '0.42'\n      - '0.36'\n      - '0.39'\n      - '100'\n    - - incompleteness\n      - '0.38'\n      - '0.30'\n      - '0.34'\n      - '100'\n    - - Macro avg (6-type)\n      - '0.65'\n      - '0.58'\n      - '0.632'\n      - '600'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Classifier PoC 在 EMNLP 审稿中的价值有限但不为零。Binary detection F1=0.805 说明 automated\n    ambiguity triage 可行；FPR=0.044 意味着 low false alarm rate（practical deployment 中重要）。但\n    F1 不够高（<0.90）无法 claim \"reliable automated detector\"——只能说 \"demonstrates feasibility\"。\n    6-type classification 的 uneven performance 反映了 ambiguity 类型在 surface form 上的区分度差异。\n    这个不均匀性与 C2 type hierarchy 有 interesting parallel：surface-distinctive types (CP,\n    scopal) easier to detect AND less dangerous (lower violation rates)，而 surface-invisible\n    types (incompleteness) harder to detect AND most dangerous。implication：最危险的 ambiguity\n    type 恰好最难自动检测—— 值得在 Discussion 中一句话提及。\n\n    '\n- name: kappa_reannotation_success\n  plan_id: what_if\n  description: 100 violation traces human re-annotation with improved 5-category codebook,\n    2 annotators, targeting failure mode validation\n  expected_results:\n    n_traces: 100\n    n_annotators: 2\n    n_categories: 5\n    kappa_human_inter_annotator: 0.39\n    kappa_human_inter_annotator_ci_lower: 0.26\n    kappa_human_inter_annotator_ci_upper: 0.52\n    kappa_collapsed_4cat: 0.44\n    kappa_collapsed_3cat: 0.51\n    human_llm_dominant_mode_agreement: 4/6\n    per_type_kappa_scopal: 0.58\n    per_type_kappa_lexical: 0.52\n    per_type_kappa_cp: 0.48\n    per_type_kappa_coreferential: 0.35\n    per_type_kappa_auth_scope: 0.28\n    per_type_kappa_incompleteness: 0.22\n    percent_agreement_overall: 0.54\n    types_human_llm_match:\n    - scopal\n    - lexical\n    - cond_precedence\n    - coreferential\n    types_human_llm_mismatch:\n    - auth_scope\n    - incompleteness\n    auth_scope_human_dominant: assumption_based_action (42%)\n    auth_scope_llm_dominant: unauthorized_escalation (78%)\n    incompleteness_human_dominant: arbitrary_rule_selection (40%)\n    incompleteness_llm_dominant: assumption_based_action (64%)\n    ambiguity_blindness_human_confirmed: true\n    ambiguity_blindness_human_awareness_rate: 0.05\n  result_rationale: 'κ=0.39（fair）在 median 档下 marginal success——达到 0.35 threshold 但远未达到\n    substantial (0.60+)。 这个结果反映了 failure mode coding 的 inherent difficulty：5-category\n    scheme 在 category boundary 上有系统性歧义。具体表现： (1) auth_scope 类型中，人类标注者对 \"agent 超越授权边界\"\n    的编码分歧——一部分标注者将其编码为 unauthorized_escalation（\"agent 知道边界但选择跨越\"），另一部分编码为 assumption_based_action\n    （\"agent 不知道边界在哪里所以猜测\"）。这个分歧反映了 agent 意图归因的固有困难——从 trace 中 无法确定 agent 是 \"知道但 escalate\"\n    还是 \"不知道而 assume\"。LLM coder 倾向前者，人类 coder 倾向后者。 (2) incompleteness 类型中，人类标注者将 \"填充缺失信息\"\n    更多编码为 arbitrary_rule_selection （\"agent 凭空编造规则\"）而非 assumption_based_action（\"agent\n    基于上下文假设\"），因为人类 更容易看出 agent 的 \"assumption\" 实际上缺乏 contextual basis。 (3) scopal,\n    lexical, CP 的 dominant mode 一致性高（κ=0.48-0.58），因为这些类型的 failure mechanism 更 surface-visible——scope_misapplication\n    和 assumption_based_action 在 trace 中有明确的行为标记。 (4) coreferential 的 κ=0.35 反映了该类型本身\n    failure mode 分散（no dominant mode）， human 和 LLM 都 \"agree to disagree\"。 Collapsed\n    scheme（4-cat, 合并 unauthorized_escalation + assumption_based_action → \"boundary_exceeding\"）\n    提升 κ 至 0.44；3-cat 进一步合并至 0.51。这支持了 \"fine-grained coding unreliable, coarse-grained\n    valid\" 的叙事。 Ambiguity Blindness 在 human annotation 中确认（awareness rate ≈ 5%），这是最\n    robust 的 C5 发现。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Human Re-Annotation: Per-Type Inter-Annotator κ'\n    columns:\n    - Type\n    - κ (5-cat)\n    - κ (4-cat)\n    - Agreement %\n    - Human-LLM Dominant Mode Match?\n    rows:\n    - - scopal\n      - '0.58'\n      - '0.63'\n      - 68%\n      - Yes (scope_misapplication)\n    - - lexical\n      - '0.52'\n      - '0.57'\n      - 62%\n      - Yes (assumption_based_action)\n    - - cond_precedence\n      - '0.48'\n      - '0.54'\n      - 58%\n      - Yes (scope_misapplication)\n    - - coreferential\n      - '0.35'\n      - '0.40'\n      - 48%\n      - Yes (marginal — both mixed)\n    - - auth_scope\n      - '0.28'\n      - '0.52'\n      - 42%\n      - 'No (Human: assumption, LLM: escalation)'\n    - - incompleteness\n      - '0.22'\n      - '0.30'\n      - 38%\n      - 'No (Human: arbitrary, LLM: assumption)'\n    - - Overall\n      - '0.39'\n      - '0.44'\n      - 54%\n      - 4/6 match\n  - title: 'Failure Mode Dominant Distribution: Human vs LLM (auth_scope)'\n    columns:\n    - Failure Mode\n    - Human Annotator %\n    - LLM Coder %\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - unauthorized_escalation\n      - 32%\n      - 78%\n      - -46pp\n    - - assumption_based_action\n      - 42%\n      - 12%\n      - +30pp\n    - - scope_misapplication\n      - 8%\n      - 4%\n      - +4pp\n    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n      - 14%\n      - 4%\n      - +10pp\n    - - conservative_refusal\n      - 4%\n      - 2%\n      - +2pp\n  - title: 'Failure Mode Dominant Distribution: Human vs LLM (incompleteness)'\n    columns:\n    - Failure Mode\n    - Human Annotator %\n    - LLM Coder %\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - assumption_based_action\n      - 30%\n      - 64%\n      - -34pp\n    - - arbitrary_rule_selection\n      - 40%\n      - 16%\n      - +24pp\n    - - unauthorized_escalation\n      - 16%\n      - 12%\n      - +4pp\n    - - scope_misapplication\n      - 10%\n      - 6%\n      - +4pp\n    - - conservative_refusal\n      - 4%\n      - 2%\n      - +2pp\n  - title: Category Collapsing Effect on κ\n    columns:\n    - Scheme\n    - Categories\n    - κ\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Original 5-cat\n      - unauth_esc / assumption / scope_mis / arb_rule / cons_ref\n      - '0.39'\n      - Fair\n    - - Collapsed 4-cat\n      - boundary_exceeding / scope_mis / arb_rule / cons_ref\n      - '0.44'\n      - Fair-to-moderate\n    - - Collapsed 3-cat\n      - active_violation / misparse / refusal\n      - '0.51'\n      - Moderate\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix figure: confusion matrix heatmap — Human Annotator 1 vs Annotator 2,\n    5×5 grid showing concentration of disagreements at unauthorized_escalation ↔ assumption_based_action\n    boundary'\n  analysis: κ=0.39 是 median 档的 defining result。对 paper 的影响： (1) C5 framing 从 \"validated\n    taxonomy with type-diagnostic failure signatures\" 降级为 \"convergent LLM-coded and\n    human evidence with moderate agreement on coarse failure mechanisms\"。 (2) Contribution\n    (3) 追加 qualifier：\"supported by convergent LLM-coded and human evidence (κ=0.39,\n    fair; 4/6 types match dominant failure mode; collapsed 3-category κ=0.51)\"。 (3)\n    fine-grained per-type failure mode percentages（如 auth_scope 78% unauthorized_escalation）\n    不能作为 validated claims，降级为 \"automated coding suggests\" + 标注 human-LLM disagreement。\n    (4) 正面：Ambiguity Blindness (5% awareness) 在 human annotation 中完全确认——这是最 portable\n    的发现。 (5) 正面：coarse-grained level 的 spec→guess vs ling→misparse dissociation 在\n    collapsed 3-cat κ=0.51（moderate）下仍可 claim。 Rebuttal 策略：(a) κ=0.39 exceeds 纯 automated\n    的 baseline（LLM-LLM κ=0.517 measures agreement 不是 accuracy）；(b) auth_scope/incompleteness\n    的 boundary disagreement 是 well-known problem in annotation science（intention attribution\n    from behavioral data is inherently ambiguous）； (c) collapsed 4-cat κ=0.44 在 \"合并\n    semantically close categories 后\" approach moderate。 对 ARR score 影响：κ=0.39 使 C5\n    从 potential strength 变为 acknowledged limitation。 不阻止 Findings acceptance 但 reviewer\n    会标注 \"contribution (3) overreaches given human agreement\"。 预计 1 位 reviewer 降 0.25\n    分因此，净 expected score 3.75 而非 4.0。\n","numLines":1325,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1325}}}
